{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions","id":677864,"title":"There are only 100 sidereals...so how are there so many factions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-25T12:53:43-07:00","id":677864,"title":"There are only 100 sidereals...so how are there so many factions?","content":"There are but 100 Sidereals at any one time. Never any more, never any less. However, there are a ridiculous amount of factions and pseudo-factions nonetheless:<br /> <br /> Gold Faction<br /> Bronze Faction<br /> Independents<br /> Silver Faction<br /> Ronin<br /> Rakan Thulio<br /> <br /> Adding to this, the Bronze Faction is said to comprise the vast majority of Sids. So, if there's, say, 70 Bronze Faction guys, then that leaves only 30 for everyone else. Taking out Rakan, then you have 29. The Gold Faction has to have at least, say, 15, so you're telling me that the Independents, Silver Faction, and Ronin make do with the remaining 14? Unless the Gold Faction isn't a plurality of the Sids total, it just has the most members of all of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T12:57:00-07:00","id":677891,"title":"","content":"Ronins aren't a faction. A ronin is literally one person doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> Raken Thulio is part of 3.0 and we don't know how many Sidereals there will be that edition. However, the Geitamins aren't Siderals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:01:37-07:00","id":677895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677891#post677891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ronins aren't a faction. A ronin is literally one person doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> Raken Thulio is part of 3.0 and we don't know how many Sidereals there will be that edition. However, the Geitamins aren't Siderals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ronin are still a group of Sidereals who share a common characteristic: they don't work for the Bureau of Destiny and don't live in Heaven. Ergo, they cannot be a part of the other factions. That's why I said &quot;Pseudo-Factions&quot;.<br /> <br /> I thought Rakan was a Sidereal who found the Getimian Exaltations somehow and decided to wage war on Heaven.<br /> <br /> Finally, I have immense doubt they'll change the number of Sids when it's so integrated into their themes that they're called the &quot;Five-Score Fellowship&quot;. No one calls the Solars the &quot;The Fifteen-Score [Whatever]&quot;. Unless 3e is gonna make &quot;Five-Score Fellowship&quot; an archaic term like &quot;Ten Thousand Dragons&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:01:55-07:00","id":677896,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Silver Faction a <i>possible</i> faction that didn't really exist? I only remember one character being at all connected with the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:04:19-07:00","id":677897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677896#post677896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the Silver Faction a <i>possible</i> faction that didn't really exist? I only remember one character being at all connected with the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2e Sids book implies that there are actual Sidereals who sometimes help the Lunars, but they aren't really a faction like the Golds and Bronzes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:06:54-07:00","id":677900,"title":"","content":"The Silver Faction is apparently at most two guys who think Lunars are really cool. They keep their Lunar dealings quiet, so they probably fall under Independent. <br /> <br /> Let's say there are about 80 Sidereals active in Yu Shan. I think the order of most Sidereals to least is Bronze (40), Independents (25) (who in my opinion individually lean Bronze or Gold, but don't have the patience for Faction politics.), and Gold (15). The other twenty are Ronin or too young to Exalt. Bronze trends towards the older Exalts while Gold Faction members tended to be newly exalted. <br /> <br /> Gold Faction is picking up members quickly since the Solars have returned. So it is possible that the numbers are more like Bronze (35), Gold (30), Independents (15). Bronze faction will lose members who were only Bronze for political reasons (and want to ride the rising Golden Star) or those who lost hope in the vision of Bronze. Gold Leaning Independents will finally commit once they see that the Solars are back in action. <br /> <br /> The actual numbers will vary based on story teller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:07:09-07:00","id":677903,"title":"","content":"Functionally, there are 2 Factions: Gold and Bronze, of which the latter holds probably a majority of Sids (maybe 60?) There are a handful of Independents at beast (the most well-known being Nazri), and I would estimate maybe 1 or 2 ronin, max, at any given time (more likely there are frequently zero).<br /> <br /> I don't recall any other Sidereals siding with Rakan Thulio, although some might be sympathetic to his concerns about Fate removing their self-determination, declaring war on Heaven marks him as a traitor regardless.<br /> <br /> Though I don't know if the whole &quot;100 Sids only&quot; thing still holds water, there's a difference between &quot;we're understaffed and overworked&quot; and &quot;we are understaffed to the point that being an effective agency is frankly absurd using any real logic, unless we have non-Sid deputies also doing stuff.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:09:44-07:00","id":677909,"title":"","content":"The factions only make sense as a driving force in Celestial politics if you extend the factions beyond just the Sidereals and out into the spirits that form the majority of staff in the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> However, the game line has always acknowledged the small number of Sidereals in the factions. The &quot;Silver Faction&quot; is two guys who have occasionally helped the Lunars in exchange for favors. Rakan Thulio seems to be waging his war on Heaven without other Sidereals. The Bronze Faction has more membership than the Gold Faction, but no numbers are ever given. Those who aren't part of any of the above are either Independants or Ronin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:14:23-07:00","id":677914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677909#post677909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The factions only make sense as a driving force in Celestial politics if you extend the factions beyond just the Sidereals and out into the spirits that form the majority of staff in the Bureau of Destiny.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. I'd include all Gods in the Gold/Bronze/Independent Divide. Celestial Politics are much more interesting if you look beyond Sidereals as the only participants and throw out the whole &quot;All Gods are Gold Faction except for a couple of exceptions.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:16:22-07:00","id":677915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677903#post677903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Functionally, there are 2 Factions: Gold and Bronze, of which the latter holds probably a majority of Sids (maybe 60?) There are a handful of Independents at beast (the most well-known being Nazri), and I would estimate maybe 1 or 2 ronin, max, at any given time (more likely there are frequently zero).<br /> <br /> I don't recall any other Sidereals siding with Rakan Thulio, although some might be sympathetic to his concerns about Fate removing their self-determination, declaring war on Heaven marks him as a traitor regardless.<br /> <br /> Though I don't know if the whole &quot;100 Sids only&quot; thing still holds water, there's a difference between &quot;we're understaffed and overworked&quot; and &quot;we are understaffed to the point that being an effective agency is frankly absurd using any real logic, unless we have non-Sid deputies also doing stuff.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm treating Rakan as a faction all to himself. He's not a Ronin because Ronin aren't hostile towards Heaven, they just don't work for it.<br /> <br /> I always assumed there would be a decent amount of Independents, mostly from post-Usurpation Exaltations who hold the mindset of &quot;this shit's all in the past, everyone, it's time to <i>let it the fuck go</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:30:50-07:00","id":677923,"title":"","content":"There are only two factions and independents.<br /> <br /> there is no silver faction, the Sidereals are at war with the Lunars.<br /> <br /> there is no Iron Faction, the Sidereals are at war with the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Rakan Thulio is one guy and therefore Independent.<br /> <br /> Ronin is not a faction, its a state of ignorance. they're all independents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:46:21-07:00","id":677935,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the total numbers are probably somewhere around 55 Bronze Faction Sidereal, 20 Gold Faction Sidereal and 25 Others (including Ronin, those working with Thulio, those who actually are independent, young Sidereal who haven't Exalted yet, possible members who have some other philosophy that doesn't want to see Solars or Dragon Blooded in control of Creation, etc). <br /> <br /> Prior to the release of the Solar Exalted, the vast majority of Sidereals were claimed as members of the Bronze Faction, there was no Gold Faction and only a small handful of Sidereal were Independent. Once the Solars came back, some of the older Independents chose to side with the Gold Faction. Meanwhile younger members of the Bronze Faction, who would have to centuries to get anywhere in the faction either decided to join the Gold Faction, or go Independent and functionally develop ties to both factions (sort of like a mercenary) so that they can play a pivotal role in the future of the Five-score Botherhood and turn that into power and influence down the road, regardless of which faction wins.<br /> <br /> While the Bronze Faction still contains a majority of the Sidereal, and it tries to paint itself as being the most powerful, the reality is that it's position has slipped quite a bit and could very quickly be chipped away depending on what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:49:59-07:00","id":677937,"title":"","content":"There's so many factions the same way the Blessed Isle book says there's 5 sidereals who spend most of their time guarding Mount Meru from mortals climbing it's slopes - AKA some writers don't grok how few Sidereals there are in comparison to how big Creation is and/or they don't understand how delegation works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:55:31-07:00","id":677942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677937#post677937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's so many factions the same way the Blessed Isle book says there's 5 sidereals who spend most of their time guarding Mount Meru from mortals climbing it's slopes - AKA some writers don't grok how few Sidereals there are in comparison to how big Creation is and/or they don't understand how delegation works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The writers sprinkle Sidereals all of Creation and if you add them up, there isn't enough Sidereals for missions/Wyld Hunt. I just chalk it up as &quot;Well, there could be Sidereals here, Storyteller. If it doesn't work with your game, then don't put them here!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T14:15:08-07:00","id":677986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677915#post677915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm treating Rakan as a faction all to himself. He's not a Ronin because Ronin aren't hostile towards Heaven, they just don't work for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ronin could certainly be hostile to Heaven. Ronin aren't defined by loyalty or lack of aggression, but by &quot;I'm not part of your system, and in all likelihood probably know nothing about it anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Independent&quot; typically means &quot;I'm doing my job but I'm not interested in your elephant vs donkey bullshit over there.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677915#post677915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed there would be a decent amount of Independents, mostly from post-Usurpation Exaltations who hold the mindset of &quot;this shit's all in the past, everyone, it's time to <i>let it the fuck go</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-Usurpation Sids should be vanishingly rare. Under ten of them, if that. Sids have a nasty tendency to get their asses killed by Lunars. Lunars don't give a shit what faction you are; you've been conducting a pogrom-by-proxy against them for over two millennia, ergo you all have blood on your hands, even if it was from a previous life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T14:30:54-07:00","id":677998,"title":"","content":"You can get about three or four factions in the representatives of a single political party in a legislature. I just finished watching Lincoln again, a film covering a real life event in which much of the tension comes from needing to rally a cohesive political action out of Republicans divided between Conservative, Radical, and those loyal to Lincoln, a group consisting of, what, 120 people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T16:06:08-07:00","id":678178,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Sidereals. My boys!<br /> <br /> Anyway. Here's the thing. The non-Gold, non-Bronze Sidereal &quot;factions&quot;, such as they might or might not still exist in 3e, basically boil down to &quot;two or three guys with radical views who keep it to themselves.&quot; Those two or three guys might have a lot of subtle power in Creation, but until such time as they put together a big enough coup to sell to their brethren, they're less a faction than they are those weird guys in the office who are always muttering about this killer presentation they'll deliver one day but never quite get around to it.<br /> <br /> Everyone is talking about numbers, so I'll throw out my own. Strap in: I have <i>thoughts</i> on this. Everything that follows is simply <i>how I do it</i>, not necessarily, unless stated, how it <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> I usually assume that at any given time, there are about 80 Sidereals active. Cutting their numbers by a fifth sounds harsh, but keep in mind I'm lumping every single inactive Sidereal into that; people who are between Exaltations, guys on leave, Ronin, in 3e Rakan Thulio, people who just got their arm bitten off by a Lunar and maybe need some convalescent time, guys detached for a special independent project they can't easily be recalled from, etc. 80 might even be generous, but it seems fair.<br /> <br /> The Directional Conventions (Capital, Fire, Wood, Water, Air) I figure have about 20 guys in Capital and 12 or so in the other directional Conventions at any given time. It's explicit that the Bronze Faction keeps Capital more heavily staffed in order to ensure that everything in the Realm, which is sort of a big deal to them, remains stable. The other 12 are either in Conventions that have time commitment needs that necessitate them not also being in a Directional Convention, or are full-time in Heaven for other reasons; regardless, they probably spend most of their time in Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> I feel it important to note that these dilineations are considerably more amorphous than I've made them and people probably drift in and out. Your Convention Chair might assign you to be this years Yu-Shan liaison officer, meaning that you spend two-thirds of the year manning the desk there and working hard on behalf of your Conventions interests and shepherding through prayer requests and sitting in on meetings, and the other third shuttling back to Creation to update your superior and meet with your fellow Convention members. Even though that guy technically has a Creation posting, he is actually in Yu-Shan most of the time. He might do well enough there that the Bureau of Destiny transfers him to Yu-Shan full time to be their in-house liaison with one of the other Bureaus, or he might be cycled back to Creation and spend five years humping through the southern deserts hunting Fair Folk and never seeing Yu-Shan because Nazri thinks he could be the next great raksha troubleshooter and wants to give him some much-needed seasoning.<br /> <br /> Similarly, someone who supposedly has a full-time Heaven billet might actually spend most of their time in Creation; the senior Sidereal whose job is literally &quot;be a Sifu&quot; might spend all of his time visiting his students in Creation and training them while they go about their duties. That's his full-time job, passing down the techniques of the Five-Score Fellowship to the next generation. It would be nice to have them all in Yu-Shan at the dojo, but not often feasible.<br /> <br /> (This might also apply to, say, a Bronze Faction member who is given a ridiculously easy desk job in Yu-Shan to cover up the fact that he's really teaching sorcery at the Heptagram. Despite his billet in Heaven, that dude is basically living in Creation.)<br /> <br /> So them's the broad strokes. Let's talk Faction numbers.<br /> <br /> A lot of people like to give the Bronze Faction overwhelming numerical superiority. That's a way to go. It's an effective way to go, dramatic even, especially if you're running a game where you want to see the Gold Faction suddenly snowball out of control and get a horde of defections.<br /> <br /> Not how I go. The split I usually use, in order to maintain canon compliance with there being more Bronze than Gold, is 30/25/25, Bronze/Gold/Independent. I move that around somewhat but that's a good ballpark.<br /> <br /> This is because I prefer the Bronze Faction strength, and Gold Faction weakness, not to come via anything so gauche as weight of numbers. That's not very... Sidereal. Well, okay, it kind of is in some ways, &quot;I thought I had the votes but it turns out I was wrong&quot; is a <i>very</i> Sidereal problem to have, but... ehhh.<br /> <br /> No, I like to represent the Bronze Faction strength, and the struggles of the Gold, via bureaucratic control. The Bronze Faction only has five more dudes than the Golds, but the Bronze Faction has a disproportionate number of Sidereal Elders (I have never run a game with a living pre-Usurpation Sidereal who was <i>not</i> an ardent Bronze) and occupies a disproportionate number of important posts and has a disproportionate number of friends and favors among the gods and spirits.<br /> <br /> So they can do more with less. They can arrange assignments for their members that perfectly overlap with faction business, killing two birds with one stone. They can get their hands on awesome gear, magic when needed, divine intervention when necessary. The Gold, in turn, actually punch BELOW the weight class their numbers indicate, because they occupy a disproportionately smaller number of plum positions and so have to work twice as hard for half the result.<br /> <br /> That's how I model Bronze having the upper hand. It should not, in my opinion, be a matter of &quot;there's just so many of us&quot; but rather &quot;we've been here forever and you, my young and idealistic friend, have <i>not</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677903#post677903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I don't know if the whole &quot;100 Sids only&quot; thing still holds water, there's a difference between &quot;we're understaffed and overworked&quot; and &quot;we are understaffed to the point that being an effective agency is frankly absurd using any real logic, unless we have non-Sid deputies also doing stuff.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>... presumably they do? The Bureau of Destiny is, I've always assumed, actually majority NON-Sidereal. They probably have tons and tons of gods working there who do stuff. The Sidereals are only called in when stuff falls within their specific ambit, which is still a shit-ton of stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The factions only make sense as a driving force in Celestial politics if you extend the factions beyond just the Sidereals and out into the spirits that form the majority of staff in the Bureau of Destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, kinda? I mean, keep in mind the Sidereals have direct promotion paths into the upper management levels of the BoD. If your big-shot boss is a rabid faction partisan, you may suddenly decide you care very much indeed about factional politics. Same deal with the wunderkind you're working with who you get the feeling might be promoted any time this century.<br /> <br /> I'd never really thought about that aspect before, mostly because I've largely treated the Sidereals by themselves as having a lot of force majeur and also of them not really fucking with the other Bureaus unless absolutely necessary. They'll certainly become involved with them over the course of normal Heavenly politics, of course, but they're not going to launch major unprovoked initiatives against them, if for no other reason than that's <i>so much work</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T16:39:14-07:00","id":678251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=678178#post678178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... presumably they do? The Bureau of Destiny is, I've always assumed, actually majority NON-Sidereal. They probably have tons and tons of gods working there who do stuff. The Sidereals are only called in when stuff falls within their specific ambit, which is still a shit-ton of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think this is probably true, the books have never done this justice (beyond &quot;X is a strident Bronze supporter god,&quot; I mean, that's only so useful when it discusses one Bronze-supporter-god versus, say, the kinds of gods generally allying with and working under the bronze Sids and who frequently do the majority of the Bureau's work and troubleshooting) and it leads to the whole implausible notion of &quot;Sids do everything&quot; which goes so far beyond &quot;overworked.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell a fun couple missions for Sids could be &quot;do the political and bureaucratic maneuvering and paperwork to ensure these guys get on our payroll because they'll be more effective agents if they're actually our subordinates instead of basically contractors.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T16:50:21-07:00","id":678292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=678251#post678251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell a fun couple missions for Sids could be &quot;do the political and bureaucratic maneuvering and paperwork to ensure these guys get on our payroll because they'll be more effective agents if they're actually our subordinates instead of basically contractors.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>... you know, now I really want to run a game where some bright spark in Yu-Shan gets the brilliant idea of exploiting the underclass of unemployed deities in a kind of day labor system. I'm imagining a cirrus skiff rolling into the bad part of town and loading up guys onto the back of it like migrant workers outside a Home Depot during fruit-picking season, carting them off to the Bureaus or to Creation to do divine scut work for a few days or weeks before dumping them back into Heaven with a paltry amount of ambrosia for their troubles.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals would be very, very torn between doing something about that and realizing they now have some <i>completely deniable</i> budget manpower at their disposal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T17:50:54-07:00","id":678342,"title":"","content":"Actually, considering the aforementioned film, I'm suddenly struck by the idea that the incongruity a lot of people are getting is from thinking of them in terms of the factions of a country torn apart by civil war as opposed to within elected representatives of the same party. I don't really understand why, since the Sidereals basically have all of the features (the structure laid out for the Bronze Faction in both Sidereal books is almost exactly what you would expect of the kinds of old boys clubs that spring up in certain parties) and I think almost everybody here would come from countries in which factionalised party politics has at least been a historical thing, but never mind. Regardless, it's very easy to have at least two and maybe up to four or five divisions within even a relatively small (but still sizable) group that is tight-knit and politically oriented as a matter of course. Take several dozen people who are all about Deciding Things and have them able to split up and fill a couple of large rooms along lines of Different Decisions, and you've got some factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T19:11:04-07:00","id":678399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions#post677864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are there so many factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how to answer this question without being a little sarcastic. The Exalted are demigods Chosen because of their adherence to world-changing goals and typified by intense passions, made supernaturally persuasive by dint of being Exalted. I am not at all surprised a hundred of them can come up with quite a few differing ideologies to believe in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:22:11-07:00","id":678445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=677986#post677986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-Usurpation Sids should be vanishingly rare. Under ten of them, if that. Sids have a nasty tendency to get their asses killed by Lunars. Lunars don't give a shit what faction you are; you've been conducting a pogrom-by-proxy against them for over two millennia, ergo you all have blood on your hands, even if it was from a previous life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer to think that Lunars are varied in their own political and ideological views just as much as Sidereals. They'd presumably all oppose the Wyld Hunt, Immaculate lies, and the supporters of those. But their capacity for mercy towards random Sidereals who don't seem to be attacking them/helping the Immaculates should vary.<br /> <br /> Also, I really sincerely doubt any non-Sidereal is at all aware of the Gold Faction as a political group, except Cult of the Illuminated members. Even if (as I prefer to think) the faction was revived after the Contagion instead of overnight in R.Y. 763. They are more likely to be aware of the concept of ronin as a hypothetical that could potentially be exploited or influenced -- especially if they know of the Getimians' war against Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:56:43-07:00","id":678466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=678178#post678178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... presumably they do? The Bureau of Destiny is, I've always assumed, actually majority NON-Sidereal. They probably have tons and tons of gods working there who do stuff. The Sidereals are only called in when stuff falls within their specific ambit, which is still a shit-ton of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that's the impression I got from MoEP:Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Also, in 3E there will be <i>at least one </i>Getimian working for the Bureau of Destiny (Apkallu, a <i>special consultant</i>).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T23:28:37-07:00","id":678590,"title":"","content":"These are <i>Sidereals</i>, man. Don't kid yourself, there are 100 factions, even the tiny baby Sidereal-to-be who hasn't figured out solid food is his own Sidereal faction, he just doesn't know it yet. (Milk Faction?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T03:08:26-07:00","id":678690,"title":"","content":"One ameliorating factor here is that these are Sidereals, and belonging to one faction would be far too simple for them. Bronze faction member who has been in deep cover for a century? Definitely. Gold Faction member who is playing an Independent who is sympathetic to the Silver guys to gain their support? Oh yes. Double and triple and even quadruple agents? Hell yeah. <br /> <br /> When you take into account a political landscape that resembles Cold War-era espionage, things get a lot more interesting, and believable. Two large factions, with various minor and sub-factions attached, and almost everyone playing multiple sides of the game. So, sure the Independent's coffee breaks have twenty people show up, but who knows which ones are the actual Independents? Hell, one of the people might show up publicly as a Bronze Faction member to shoot the breeze, but they actually have been leaning Independent for a while now, and they want an Elder patron to cover their butts when they tell their Bronzie Sifu to screw off. Then sixty people show up to the Bronze planning meetings, but Kejak breaks them out into working groups anyway, and lets those group leaders worry about security. Even he can't keep full track of who is working with whom to betray whom anymore.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, these people DO work together, so all this intrigue and insanity results in careers setback and ruined, audits and improper raises, and every once in a while, someone ends up dead. That's really rare, because even most of the hardcore Bronzies are not willing to straight up murder a &quot;Gold Star&quot; whose help they might need to save their ass on official business.<br /> <br /> So all of this crap goes nowhere...for centuries. Then the Solars come back, and shit gets real. That's the perfect moment for PC Sids to either pull a masterstroke of intrigue, OR to cut though all the BS and say &quot;Hey, bros, we gotta set aside this Heptagram love triangle Yeddim shit and get stuff done.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR Many Sid factions work when you realize many of them don't belong to just one faction, effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T04:35:42-07:00","id":678787,"title":"","content":"that makes sense, Totentanz. Perhaps that explains the Iron Faction: its not a real faction, its just the obligatory &quot;flock of wolves&quot; faction that is composed entirely of betrayers or infiltrators trying to spy on the Iron Faction, the concept of an Iron faction itself being just some rumor some Gold faction Sidereal started to distract the Bronzes from their activities, and some Sidereals put too much effort into finding, so of course its composed of a Bronze, Independent and a Gold all sharing what they know of their own factions and pretending to plot against them, but since all their real goals are to preserve Creation, none of them make any moves to actually do anything in favor of the Underworld and keep making excuses as to why not.<br /> <br /> and of course the gods have their own politics as well and the Sidereals are furthermore probably multiply involved in those in some manner.<br /> <br /> as well being on multiple conventions, probably.<br /> <br /> on top of any other jobs the Celestial Bureaucracy decides to hand them.<br /> <br /> and is probably going down into Creation making resplendent destinies.<br /> <br /> and somehow finds time to train themselves in martial arts.<br /> <br /> ....at some point you realize that the average Sidereal is so busy playing multi-agent that a major theme for them might be loyalty. namely....what is a Sidereal truly loyal to? They're taken from their homes early and trained for years to be a Sidereal, they are taught to think of the good of Creation in general above wherever they came from, their arcane fate, occluding them from mortal memory keeps them from forming any kind of lasting relationship with the rest of humanity, they have to deal with various gods around them who will only care for them as far as politics or getting certain jobs in fate done, their peers are divided into ideologies that seem more of a hinder than help, and the only non-political relationship they might develop is with a Sifu, a student-teacher role, and the factions only make sense if they make all that worse by constantly playing multiple sides and trying to betray one another. the whole set up seems deliberately designed to make the Sidereal Exaltation a lonely existence with no clear ways to obtain meaningful trusting relationships. No wonder the Sidereals might band together so tightly as to be called the Five-Score Fellowship: they know that they're the only people who can truly understand one another and what their job entails, so they try to form close tight-knit bonds as much as they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T09:36:07-07:00","id":679125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=678787#post678787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that makes sense, Totentanz. Perhaps that explains the Iron Faction: its not a real faction, its just the obligatory &quot;flock of wolves&quot; faction that is composed entirely of betrayers or infiltrators trying to spy on the Iron Faction, the concept of an Iron faction itself being just some rumor some Gold faction Sidereal started to distract the Bronzes from their activities, and some Sidereals put too much effort into finding, so of course its composed of a Bronze, Independent and a Gold all sharing what they know of their own factions and pretending to plot against them, but since all their real goals are to preserve Creation, none of them make any moves to actually do anything in favor of the Underworld and keep making excuses as to why not.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/6d/95/60/6d956067fbad1cc8e277c7e8b15db66d.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....at some point you realize that the average Sidereal is so busy playing multi-agent that a major theme for them might be loyalty. namely....what is a Sidereal truly loyal to? </div> </div> </div>Why, their own <i><b>stupendous</b></i> egos, of course! Nobody else is trustworthy or competent, after all.<br /> <br /> They're politicians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T09:49:28-07:00","id":679131,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer early 1e where the five guys who made up the Gold Faction went Ronin around the time of the Usurpation. Thus, the whole Bronze/Gold thing pretty much doesn't exist and, presumably, everyone has moved on to political issues that are actually <i>important</i> these days. Yes, it can be assumed that the majority of the Sidereal Host follows Chejop and Co., supports the Realm, and will hunt and kill Solars, but there are lots of other politics involved, some people going ronin, others trying to reach out to the Gold faction, etc.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the &quot;Gold Faction&quot; are a few Elder Ronin, still wanted by the Sidereal Host. If you're a Solar, if no one else can help, and if you can find them, maybe you can be trained by a Sidereal Master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T09:50:01-07:00","id":679132,"title":"","content":"I don't read the Gold and Bronze Factions as just Sidereals. &quot;The Bronze Faction&quot; in general has applied to those who in Heaven who rose to the top through the Usurpation - so it can be applied to Ryzala as much as Chejop. By the same logic, &quot;Gold Faction&quot; can apply to the Syndics as much as Ayesha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T09:58:31-07:00","id":679134,"title":"","content":"I will never understand why some people opt to take the prominence of the dichotomy between Bronze and Gold as indicating that that is the sole issue of which they are concerned. Dear God do they need the Getimians, their responsibility in managing the Exigents and the more active hatred of the Lunars to remind people of them still having plenty of things that they are both all together in and can have divisions on policy that are not directly composed of the Bronze/Gold dichotomy (although may still inform some of their ideas on why they should be issues; &quot;my, this latest Lunar disaster might not have happened if we hadn't overthrown the Solars, eh? Maybe working towards bringing them back might help heal that rift? Something to think about?&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T12:56:20-07:00","id":679276,"title":"","content":"[insert comparison to US Democratic and Republican parties]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:13:31-07:00","id":679290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679276#post679276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[insert comparison to US Democratic and Republican parties]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a better comparison would be to look earlier than our formally institutionalized parties. Think about the early US, which wasn't supposed to have parties, but the founders very quickly formed cliques between those who agreed with Hamilton and those who agreed with Jefferson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T14:14:55-07:00","id":679324,"title":"","content":"I have found it helpful during my games to downplay official &quot;factions.&quot; I portray it more along the lines of the Christian/atheist divide, where it's more like there's groups of sympathizers but there are still differing philosophies within each faction. Each head is only as powerful as he or she can convince, extort, or bargain his or her members to consent. For instance, Richard Dawkins is seen as a thought-leader for many atheists, but there are still some who disagree with him and no one would really say he's &quot;in charge&quot; of atheists. Likewise, Martin Luther was a revolutionary Protestant, but he didn't seek to become an Anti-Pope; he was just a loud, convincing voice. A simpler (and clumsier) comparison would be the same structure most high schools have with jocks and nerds. No one is in charge of either group, but there is definitely a top jock and a top nerd.<br /> <br /> Similarly, most of the Bronze Faction believes Chejop has the right idea: oppose Anathema. Some are willing to take it to the length of forecasting Solar Exaltations and murdering their new hosts. Others seek to guide the Wyld Hunt to harry and harass the surviving Solars to the edges of Creation. Some still seek a way to strengthen the Scarlet Empire to be able to withstand all threats and views the &quot;hunting&quot; of Solars to be distasteful.<br /> <br /> The Gold Faction has some members that assassinate the most prominent and zealous of the Terrestrial Exalted; others seek to train the Solars and unleash them back upon Creation to remake the grand society of the First Age. Still others seek to establish academies or mentor-student relationships that will permit their wise dominance over their Solar brethren.<br /> <br /> Something both factions have in common is that it's a good idea to coordinate efforts with their own fellow believers, but they aren't beholden by any sort of pact or unified organization. There's not even a voting system in place; it's more along the lines of those who believe Utopia is achievable vs. those who believe man is inherently evil and untrustworthy as individuals.<br /> <br /> At least that's been what's fun for my game. It gives individual Sidereals a lot more free agency and permits me to come up with more nuanced NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5706-zeal","name":"Zeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T14:54:50-07:00","id":679348,"title":"","content":"Something I like from the opening comic in Manual: Sidereals is how we're given a group of Sidereals who are explicitly members of either faction, evidently fairly low down on their respective totem poles, and it thus amounts to some light, though cutting, ribbing at each others' expense, without really affecting their jobs. Although I suppose there have been people who complained about that as well: &quot;oh, members of either faction should be at each others' throats, not working together on a mutual issue&quot;, &quot;hey, you can't humanise people by having them occasionally be light-hearted about major ideological divisions, that undermines my sense of this being a game of epic epicness&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T15:22:48-07:00","id":679378,"title":"","content":"Pfft. Mercury Faction is best faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T15:35:53-07:00","id":679391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679348#post679348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I like from the opening comic in Manual: Sidereals is how we're given a group of Sidereals who are explicitly members of either faction, evidently fairly low down on their respective totem poles, and it thus amounts to some light, though cutting, ribbing at each others' expense, without really affecting their jobs. Although I suppose there have been people who complained about that as well: &quot;oh, members of either faction should be at each others' throats, not working together on a mutual issue&quot;, &quot;hey, you can't humanise people by having them occasionally be light-hearted about major ideological divisions, that undermines my sense of this being a game of epic epicness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Also on this subject... when it comes to the factions being at each others throats, it doesn't help that one of the most prominent Bronze Faction functionaries we've ever seen fleshed out in an explicitly &quot;this is a faction partisan&quot; way is Ahn-Aru.<br /> <br /> Now, I love Sad Ivory. Love her. But, well... she's somewhat <i>zealous, </i>isn't she? She murdered another Sidereal to forward her faction goals, which is something that's pretty extreme. That's fine and all, there should be faction partisans who are willing to go that far, and part of the structure of the setting is that Sidereals are now in a position where the faction goals go from &quot;theory&quot; to &quot;deadly,&quot; and the question of &quot;you may need to murder your friends and co-workers in order to make your vision for Creation come true; <i>will you</i>?&quot; is quite salient.<br /> <br /> But she's the only one who has gotten that sort of play. The other Sidereals we've seen have either been fleshed out in non-faction ways, or fleshed out in ways that involve faction politics but don't actually involve directly going at other Sidereals. When Crimson Banner Executioner showed up to save Elias' bacon, he didn't need to kill his co-workers to do it. The only example we've seen of them actually facing each other down is... well, Ahn-Aru. There ought to be less stabby examples.<br /> <br /> As for parallels of the Sidereals to political parties or cliques of elected representatives... I'm not sure that's quite right, especially ones in western democracies. Political parties of that nature are often alliances of near-equals with independent power bases with limited ability to directly compel each other. A sitting U.S Senator, for example, doesn't really effectively answer to anyone but the voters of his state; he can tell all 99 other Senators to go fuck themselves sideways, and he still gets his vote in the Senate and can actually probably still keep getting elected; Senators often have fund-raising and political machines in place that are completely divorced from the formal party structure. This sort of weak control means that the way the people in the institution self-organize in order to solve collective action problems is different than it would be in a strict hierarchy, where, say, the Majority Leader could actually issue orders to other Senators.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals <i>do </i>exist in a hierarchical, authoritarian organization. They have a great deal of freedom because of the nature of their work but they have jobs and superiors and are expected to obey orders and answer for their actions. They can be promoted, demoted, have their pay cut, assigned shitty tasks or desireable ones. The faction politics are theoretically things that happen &quot;off the clock&quot; but they intersect with their day job heavily and the factions will often expect them to do things that aren't necessarily in line with Bureau policy.<br /> <br /> The correct parallel, I feel, isn't political parties, but internal corporate politics. Or the internal politics of career (as opposed to appointed) civil service officials in one of the more hierarchically inclined ones. <i>Office</i> politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T15:55:59-07:00","id":679419,"title":"","content":"Sidereals have function and hierarchy within the Bureau, but their Fellowship amongst one another exists in a kind of distinct layer from that. I'd say that more Sidereals in the Department of Secrets are directly and formally answerable to Nara-O than they are to Chejop, even if Chejop has the prestige to do things like put pressure on their career paths. Even the Conventions... being a Chairperson is supposed to be more about setting agendas and running meetings than giving orders, I think. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Political parties of that nature are often alliances of near-equals with independent power bases with limited ability to directly compel each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know; when the venerable and beloved founder of your party makes a small gesture from the galleries, there's a lot behind why you can't disregard them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:25:09-07:00","id":679428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679419#post679419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals have function and hierarchy within the Bureau, but their Fellowship amongst one another exists in a kind of distinct layer from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely, but there's going to be a ton of intersectionality, and at least theoretically the Bureau is supposed to come first. (At least... from the Bureau's perspective.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say that more Sidereals in the Department of Secrets are directly and formally answerable to Nara-O than they are to Chejop, even if Chejop has the prestige to do things like put pressure on their career paths. </div> </div> </div>Not knowing Chejop's precise position makes things tricky, but I would argue that Chejop probably doesn't just have the &quot;prestige&quot; to put &quot;pressure&quot; on peoples career paths, he probably has formal authority to promote, demote, and re-assign people. He just probably can't nakedly exercise that power for vengeance without consequence; he has to dress it up in official clothes, because he has enemies in the office hierarchy who would fucking love to nail him for misuse of his office.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even the Conventions... being a Chairperson is supposed to be more about setting agendas and running meetings than giving orders, I think. </div> </div> </div>This would depend on the Convention, yes? Like, I imagine that the small or specialty Conventions function more like &quot;working groups,&quot; but it's always seemed pretty clear to me that the Directional Conventions, being the primary organizational unit through which the Bureau interacts with Creations, are probably run more like corporate divisions. The Convention Chairs, if they're smart, make sure all their subordinates feel like they have buy-in to the decision-making process and that their voices are heard, but when push comes to shove it seems pretty clear that the Convention Chair might need to say &quot;Your objection is noted. I'll make a formal record if you like so your ass is covered. But we've been over this ten times and you were outvoted. Get your ass to work. <i>Now</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know; when the venerable and beloved founder of your party makes a small gesture from the galleries, there's a lot behind why you can't disregard them. </div> </div> </div>That... does that happen a lot? Is Zombie Lincoln sitting in the Senate gallery working the pols? Because I might start paying more attention if that's the case.<br /> <br /> More seriously, I will admit the analogy isn't perfect, especially since the Westminster countries have radically more hierarchical political parties with more formal control over their members than the U.S does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T17:36:31-07:00","id":679480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679378#post679378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pfft. Mercury Faction is best faction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indisputably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T18:08:32-07:00","id":679495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679378#post679378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pfft. Mercury Faction is best faction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the other day I'm in Yu-Shan walking along Sunset Boulevard and Jupiter comes up to me. So I tell her, &quot;Yo. Sup?&quot;<br /> <br /> And she goes, &quot;Just letting you know I need you to vote yes at the next faction meeting.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm all, &quot;Uhhh... what faction meeting?&quot;<br /> <br /> And she says, &quot;You know, the <i>Jupiter Faction</i> meeting? The one that's scheduled in three days?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm like, &quot;Say what? There's a Jupiter Faction? When did this happen?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh,&quot; she says, &quot;You know, it was formed like 2000 years ago.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I go, &quot;Whoaa.... So there's some 2000 year old faction? And suddenly I'm part of it?&quot;<br /> <br /> And she tells me, &quot;Suddenly? You joined 400 years ago!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm like, &quot;400 years ago!? Fo shizzle!?&quot;<br /> <br /> And she nods, &quot;Fo shizzle. Anyway, since you're in charge of the Jupiter Faction, I'm just letting you know you need to vote yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I start freaking out. &quot;Wait? What? I'm in charge? I've been in charge of some faction for the last 400 years?&quot;<br /> <br /> But she goes, &quot;No silly, you were only nominated to be the man in charge 45 years ago.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm all, &quot;You mean I've been the man for the last 45 years? Damn. How come nobody ever told me I was the man?&quot;<br /> <br /> And she leans in real close and whispers, &quot;That's because it was a secret.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-26-2015, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T18:10:51-07:00","id":679496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679428#post679428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not knowing Chejop's precise position makes things tricky, but I would argue that Chejop probably doesn't just have the &quot;prestige&quot; to put &quot;pressure&quot; on peoples career paths, he probably has formal authority to promote, demote, and re-assign people. He just probably can't nakedly exercise that power for vengeance without consequence; he has to dress it up in official clothes, because he has enemies in the office hierarchy who would fucking love to nail him for misuse of his office.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's Chair of the Central Convention on Essence Use (Ayesha Ura is Chair of the Eastern Convention, which is why Sidereals are less likely to kill Solars in the Scavenger Lands than anywhere else), Chair of the Convention on Deathlords I think, controls the Wyld Hunt (which is an official, registered tool of the Bureau), and of course, is the secretary of the Mouth of Peace.<br /> So, I imagine him like Mao Tse-Tung: he's not actually President, but he's effectively the leader.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That... does that happen a lot? Is Zombie Lincoln sitting in the Senate gallery working the pols? Because I might start paying more attention if that's the case. </div> </div> </div>It does in China. A lot. Though, now the important figures are gone (like Mao, Zhou Enlai, and latterly Deng Xiao Ping), the current leader Xi Jin Ping is happy to ignore the previous leaders, and in fact is happily purging and jailing their cronies, while thumbing his nose at said previous leaders.<br /> <br /> It used to happen in Britain: John Major (PM after Thatcher) had terrible problems with, at one point, Thatcher interviewing every single government MP one-by-one and demanding they vote against their own leader (it was about a European treaty).<br /> But things have changed since then, since nowadays defeated leaders tend to fade into obscurity (in the game of Thrones, you win or you die), and the other leader who &quot;voluntarily&quot; stepped down, Tony Blair, is detested by large parts of his own party. So it doesn't really happen anymore.<br /> It's not th\u200be 1800s, where William Gladstone could leave the Conservative party, found the Liberal party, become a Chancellor under someone else who largely followed his lead, then become Prime Minister, lose, become Prime Minister again, lose, become Prime Minister again for 2 terms and then die at 82. Or Harold Wilson who did something similar in the 1960s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More seriously, I will admit the analogy isn't perfect, especially since the Westminster countries have radically more hierarchical political parties with more formal control over their members than the U.S does. </div> </div> </div>Their control isn't, officially, massively more than America, but in Britain the party provides the funding in a way that's not such a thing in America.<br /> And then there's continental countries that often have some variation of PR, which means the MPs have no independent power bases at all.<br /> <br /> Anyhow. I think your point about office politics is probably a better comparison than US politics.<br /> <br /> I'd probably compare Sidereals to the modern Chinese Communist Party though. Everyone agrees they should, and indeed must, stay in charge. Everyone agrees who they do or don't worship (for the Sidereals, the Maidens, for the CCP, no-one). Everyone publically praises the important leaders and ideology. But behind the scenes, there are multiple oblique factions. Ideological factions (ie what used to be called the Blues, Reds and Browns) crisscross with patronage groups (such as those under the protection of former leaders), and regional groups (such as the Shanghai faction). When one faction defeats another, it's not a matter of anyone being killed, it's just a matter of missing out on top jobs, being reassigned somewhere rubbish, or being told its time to retire.<br /> Until recently, when the gloves have come off, and now being on the losing side means suddenly no longer being protected from prosecution, and being sent to jail for your corruption and murders, like Bo Xilai (one of the last prominent Reds). Okay, sure, everyone's corrupt (how do you think Xi Jin Ping's family is so loaded?) but when you lose, it gets outed to the public and you go down. That never used to happen in the 90s.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-26-2015, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T23:35:46-07:00","id":679720,"title":"","content":"I think the precise amount of internecine warfare/intrigue in the Bureau is left somewhat undefined so the ST can dial it up or down to suit the story. If a group is mostly made up of Solar building a name for themselves, then perhaps the Bureau is more like the current incarnation of the US Congress, where both sides have just enough power to block each other, and nothing happens. Similarly, if the players are Sidereals, and the ST wants to build the story around their group finally breaking the factionalism and leading the Fellowship to do something big (like stopping a Deathlord), then there needs to be enough factionalism to warrant breaking it.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, if the ST is telling a story about Sids &quot;doing their day job,&quot; then he might pull the factionalism way back, to the level of Yankees and Red Sox fans working in the same office (okay, maybe not that bad). An incident like Sad Ivory murdering another Sid is considered Just Plain Wrong by everyone, Chejop included. PCs are a combination of the factions, and they mostly focus on things like stopping Getimians and fixing Loom snarls.<br /> <br /> There is also considerable room in the middle, of course. To me personally, Sids and the Bureau most resemble an intelligence apparatus. They do very important work, that often involves morally questionable, or downright loathsome things. They are all schooled to some degree in deception, intel gathering, etc. They have personal and factional agendas, oh and they live for centuries. That is a recipe for a complex web of deceit, double dealing, and schemes that operate on the scale of millennia..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:28:50-07:00","id":682200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679378#post679378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pfft. Mercury Faction is best faction.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679495#post679495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Say what? There's a Jupiter Faction?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'd like to call this meeting to order on the 467th reinstallment of the Saturn faction. My first order of business is my last, because we all know Saturn will shut this down in a little while even though she asked it to be reborn. I nominate Iron Siaka as faction head. Do I have a second?&quot;<br /> &quot;I second.&quot;<br /> &quot;Who are we killing this time?&quot;<br /> &quot;The chair does not recognize Black Ice Shadow. The motion has been seconded, please vote by roll call.&quot;<br /> &quot;Aye&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes&quot;<br /> &quot;Here&quot;<br /> &quot;I'm glad you all decided not to vote against Saturn's interpretation of Samsara, very wise. Now, we are indeed called here to plan the end of a spirit, but only because it didn't work the last time due to a lack of coordination that the Saturn faction has been reformed to remedy. Iron Siaka, take it away.&quot;<br /> &quot;You might be asking what the hell I'm doing here, but it's personal. No, I won't brief you on it. Pack up your bright morning and get ready for a trip because the Labrynth has been leaking through the Fields of Woe into Creation. Departure from the nearest gate is in 25 hours, finish up your business in Yu-Shan and don't be late.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T23:06:30-07:00","id":682687,"title":"","content":"The Venus faction of course never gets anything done, not because they waste their time on drugs and hookers as most people would think, but because they're always wasting their time with nice serene tea parties and peaceful meditation. it doesn't say Ecstasy faction after all.<br /> <br /> The Mars faction devolve into endless arguments every time they meet of course, because Mars always picks the most hot-headed disagreeable Sidereals she can as members always with polarizing views. no one knows what this faction is supposed to accomplish, because even when they do missions, they always seem to fail and breakdown into the Sidereals fighting against each other anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:23:33-07:00","id":682791,"title":"","content":"Ask two Sidereals, get three opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T02:18:14-07:00","id":682843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=679428#post679428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not knowing Chejop's precise position makes things tricky, but I would argue that Chejop probably doesn't just have the &quot;prestige&quot; to put &quot;pressure&quot; on peoples career paths, he probably has formal authority to promote, demote, and re-assign people. He just probably can't nakedly exercise that power for vengeance without consequence; he has to dress it up in official clothes, because he has enemies in the office hierarchy who would fucking love to nail him for misuse of his office.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chejop is Chair of the Central Convention and has membership in all of the special ones. I like to assign him the position of Special Adviser to Nara-O, which would be a position of extremely vague portfolio and authority even in-character, so he sometimes has direct power over Sidereals within the Department of Secrets, but everything else is all informal and based on prestige.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That... does that happen a lot? Is Zombie Lincoln sitting in the Senate gallery working the pols? Because I might start paying more attention if that's the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was making another reference to the film Lincoln, although I will admit that I had slightly misread what the position of Francis Preston Blair was. Nevertheless, he was not a Representative at the time, and yet a pivotal moment of the film has several Representatives look up into the galleries for what he wants them to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T03:35:51-07:00","id":682876,"title":"","content":"There are like... two factions. That's the smallest number of factions one can have!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T04:24:28-07:00","id":682906,"title":"","content":"Well... three if you count &quot;none of the above&quot;. And now we do have the question of what support Rakan might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:15:08-07:00","id":683008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=682876#post682876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are like... two factions. That's the smallest number of factions one can have!</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the &quot;There Are Two Factions&quot; Faction!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:31:33-07:00","id":683012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=682906#post682906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... three if you count &amp;quot;none of the above&amp;quot;. And now we do have the question of what support Rakan might have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the ones in the &quot;none of the above&quot; column count as their own coherent ideology though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:37:57-07:00","id":683015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683012#post683012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the ones in the &quot;none of the above&quot; column count as their own coherent ideology though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat akin to calling &quot;people who don't vote&quot; a &quot;political party.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T06:24:40-07:00","id":683055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=682876#post682876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are like... two factions. That's the smallest number of factions one can have!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for not reading my thread, Holden. I would have expected one of Exalted's <b>writers </b>to actually read a thread fully, but I guess some things are beyond mortal man's ability.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Oh whatever shall we do with you?</b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-30-2015, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:01:11-07:00","id":683074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683055#post683055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for not reading my thread, Holden. I would have expected one of Exalted's <b>writers </b>to actually read a thread fully, but I guess some things are beyond mortal man's ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did read your thread. Sidereals have two factions, Gold and Bronze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:20:52-07:00","id":683085,"title":"","content":"It could be that Gold and Bronze divide is more complex than Pro-Solar/Anti-Anathema. There could Bronze Faction members that up hold the Realm as the best way to protect Creation, but will not participate in Wyld Hunts unless the Anathema in question actually did something worth dying for. In contrast, there could be Gold Faction Members who disagree with the Bronze Faction handing of Celestial Politics, but still quietly feed the Wyld Hunt information on Solars.<br /> <br /> There aren't that many Sidereals where you can have a strict, &quot;Here is a check list of our Factions beliefs. Adhere to them or you are out!&quot; Even in real life, there are Liberals who are pro-firearms and conservatives that are pro-choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:46:44-07:00","id":683110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683055#post683055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for not reading my thread, Holden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frostav, I don't know how to ask this without violating the terms of use (and not the terms against personal attacks), so please take me at face value when I ask: Do you have a particular grudge against the writers? This kind of anger on your part seems like a frequently repeating pattern, and I'm just curious as to the nature of your grievance, which would not seem to...well, like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683055#post683055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have expected one of Exalted's <b>writers </b>to actually read a thread fully, but I guess some things are beyond mortal man's ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think he didn't read the thread fully? It seems to me he did and he rejected your premise (and mine) that there are a bunch of factions. What about his post makes you think he didn't read, and that his choice not to do so is based on an indifference or contempt for which he deserves to be insulted?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, for the record, I would <i>not</i> have expected one of Exalted's writers to read a thread at <i>all</i> based on the amount of hostility and pushback they tend to receive in this particular forum community, so I would ask you to please be gentler in your tone when you have an issue, because it is mortifying to me that the first post I've seen Holden make here in months is one met immediately with scorn and derision.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:26:50-07:00","id":683172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683074#post683074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He did read your thread. Sidereals have two factions, Gold and Bronze.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about just those two. There are also the independents and the Ronin (which are not a faction but by definition cannot be part of a faction). There are only <b>100</b> Sidereals, and the Bronzes apparently make up almost all of them with the Gold Faction being a tiny holdout (albeit one bolstered by the return of the Solars). How do the Bronzes not just bowl everyone else over with sheer size and plurality?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-30-2015, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:47:45-07:00","id":683211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683085#post683085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be that Gold and Bronze divide is more complex than Pro-Solar/Anti-Anathema. There could Bronze Faction members that up hold the Realm as the best way to protect Creation, but will not participate in Wyld Hunts unless the Anathema in question actually did something worth dying for. In contrast, there could be Gold Faction Members who disagree with the Bronze Faction handing of Celestial Politics, but still quietly feed the Wyld Hunt information on Solars.<br /> <br /> There aren't that many Sidereals where you can have a strict, &quot;Here is a check list of our Factions beliefs. Adhere to them or you are out!&quot; Even in real life, there are Liberals who are pro-firearms and conservatives that are pro-choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, might there be a member of the Bronze Faction who thinks Solars and Lunars are too dangerous to live, but is enough of a non-dickbag to notice and care that the current Dragon-Blooded regimes are enslaving humanity, shredding civilization in the Threshold, and utterly incapable of defending Creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:59:15-07:00","id":683219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683211#post683211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, might there be a member of the Bronze Faction who thinks Solars and Lunars are too dangerous to live, but is enough of a non-dickbag to notice and care that the current Dragon-Blooded regimes are enslaving humanity, shredding civilization in the Threshold, and utterly incapable of defending Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Political Beliefs don't have to make sense. Hell, there are probably Sidereals who are in their Sifu's Faction even though they don't believe in many of that Faction's Goals. <br /> <br /> &quot;The Dragonbloods might be assholes, but imagine how much worse a Solar/Lunar in charge would be! Have you heard of that forced beastman breeding camp the Lunars run?&quot; Complex political beliefs mean that there is a lot of backdoor dealings between Factions. Mr. Gold might give Ms. Bronze some information on a newly exalted Solar if Ms. Bronze breaks up a Realm Child Slavery Ring. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T09:07:17-07:00","id":683231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683172#post683172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about just those two. There are also the independents and the Ronin (which are not a faction but by definition cannot be part of a faction). There are only <b>100</b> Sidereals, and the Bronzes apparently make up almost all of them with the Gold Faction being a tiny holdout (albeit one bolstered by the return of the Solars). How do the Bronzes now just bowl everyone else over with <b>sheer size and plurality</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've answered your own question. I've seen groups much smaller be run by the faction that happened to have 51% of the vote. (Okay, the actual percentage was larger, because 1 person counted for more than 1% of the group, but the point still stands)<br /> <br /> Edit to add: and I've seen groups actually run by the minority, because the Minority was more organized than everyone else, and was more willing to stand up and say &quot;Okay, let's get this done!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":424,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","user":"DaWaterRat","date":". 09-30-2015, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T09:15:27-07:00","id":683236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683231#post683231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit to add: and I've seen groups actually run by the minority, because the Minority was more organized than everyone else, and was more willing to stand up and say &quot;Okay, let's get this done!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Never underestimate the ability of one person in a group to derail the whole meeting agenda by not accepting a reasonable explanation and planting seeds of doubt in the other committee member's minds.<br /> <br /> This happened in real life: <br /> Troublemaker: Why do memberships cause more when you pay with Credit Card?<br /> Reasonable Person: It's to cover the Credit Card Processing Fee. This is a common practice. <br /> Troublemaker: There is no way the Credit Card Processing Fee is two dollars. <br /> Reasonable Person: The Credit Card fee is actually $1.69, but we rounded up to two dollars to make it easier for people.<br /> Troublemaker: You are trying to make money off of the members! <br /> Reasonable Person: It's 21 cents! And you can still pay by check and not pay the credit card processing fee!<br /> Troublemaker: I don't think members should have to pay extra to use credit cards.<br /> Another Person: Maybe we should look into this more.<br /> Reasonable Person: Arg! We just voted on this six months ago!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-30-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T09:32:11-07:00","id":683243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683219#post683219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Dragonbloods might be assholes, but imagine how much worse a Solar/Lunar in charge would be! Have you heard of that forced beastman breeding camp the Lunars run?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's vastly easier to sell this after murdering everyone who actually remembers how much incomparably better most mortal quality of life and divine behavior were in the First Age. And then lying to the new recruits about how many Sidereals you murdered, what the First Age was like, and what the Great Prophecy actually said. And possibly making up some lies about how the Empress stopped the Great Contagion and &quot;of course&quot; nothing like that can ever happen again as long as she's in power.<br /> <br /> But I actually meant somebody who opposes Lunars and Solars but also recognizes that the Realm and Immaculates are hideously evil and useless to protect Creation, and wants to reform or replace them with a Dragon-Blooded regime that's actually humane and effective. Y'know, somebody who wants to make the world a better place instead of being content with how much mortals are suffering and Creation is in danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-30-2015, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T12:59:02-07:00","id":683444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683236#post683236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reasonable Person: The Credit Card fee is actually $1.69, but we rounded up to two dollars to make it easier for people.<br /> Troublemaker: You are trying to make money off of the members!<br /> Reasonable Person: It's 21 cents! And you can still pay by check and not pay the credit card processing fee!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm taking the Troublemaker side in this because they seem to be better at arithmetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683243#post683243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it's vastly easier to sell this after murdering everyone who actually remembers how much incomparably better most mortal quality of life and divine behavior were in the First Age. And then lying to the new recruits about how many Sidereals you murdered, what the First Age was like, and what the Great Prophecy actually said. And possibly making up some lies about how the Empress stopped the Great Contagion and &quot;of course&quot; nothing like that can ever happen again as long as she's in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes a canon Dreams of the First Age, or something like it.<br /> <br /> The First Age was a time of singular wonders and the incredible peaks of sorcerous ingenuity among the god-kings that ruled the world unopposed.<br /> <br /> This may not necessarily have equated to a better life among mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 09-30-2015, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:16:22-07:00","id":683460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683219#post683219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Political Beliefs don't have to make sense. Hell, there are probably Sidereals who are in their Sifu's Faction even though they don't believe in many of that Faction's Goals. <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The Dragonbloods might be assholes, but imagine how much worse a Solar/Lunar in charge would be! Have you heard of that forced beastman breeding camp the Lunars run?&amp;quot; Complex political beliefs mean that there is a lot of backdoor dealings between Factions. Mr. Gold might give Ms. Bronze some information on a newly exalted Solar if Ms. Bronze breaks up a Realm Child Slavery Ring. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That last part probably happens more than you might think, and the higher ups probably HATE it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T14:10:45-07:00","id":683542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683444#post683444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm taking the Troublemaker side in this because they seem to be better at arithmetic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mental math isn't my strong suit. You would think I'd learn to double check my numbers in internet arguments, but nooo.... I never learn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T14:51:22-07:00","id":683567,"title":"","content":"The Scarlet Dynasty is part of another reason why I was driven to find a more comprehensive image of what the Curse-addled Solars looked like, because I just don't see much credibility in the Sidereal Exalted being significantly concerned with mundane systems of oppression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:11:45-07:00","id":683582,"title":"","content":"Well sure, they're so isolated from humanity that they are unlikely to identify even remotely with mortals, or be at all concerned with what happens to them.<br /> <br /> That said... I can't find where you said it Isator but you recently posted that you thought, in spite of how awful the Deathlords are and the horrible degree of atrocities they commit, they have probably been responsible for less human suffering (in scope and scale) than the Realm and Guild. That might be true of Deathlords (especially if we leave out the Great Contagion and the Silver Prince's industrial soulsteel production) but it appears to me that it is 100% true of the ancient Solars. The worst of them committed horrible atrocities... but did not systematically reduce 99.99999% of humanity to grinding poverty with a huge side-helping of widespread chattel slavery. (They also never did anything remotely as destructive as the Great Contagion, or it would have been mentioned in a book by now. So the entire notion that the Solars the biggest possible existential threat to humanity and Creation is already utterly absurd.)<br /> <br /> It's also important to realize how unsustainable it actually is to build a society that revolves entirely around an insatiable empire that will never be satisfied with zero annual growth, whose economy is by design dependent on rapaciously draining lives and wealth out of the finite Threshold (and systematically eviscerating the capacity of Threshold civilization to defend the borders of Creation, even while being demonstrably incapable of defending the borders in their place.) The Realm is inherently unstable and unsustainable, and puts Creation into a situation that will inevitably collapse. It's no different in this regard from any imperialist or growth-dependent regime in real history, with the added problem that destabilizing, depopulating, and un-developing the Threshold is a giant, neon-sign-waving invitation to another Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> The only way I can actually imagine a worse situation, <i><b>existentially</b></i>, is to replace the Realm with people who explicitly want to destroy the world (Deathlords) or whose prime goal is to make human suffering as awful as possible (characature? of the Yozis). Though the Yozis, ironically, would be more than capable of defending Creation from (other) outside threats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It isn't reasonable for any informed Exalt, who realizes what's actually happening, to be content with Creation being destroyed unless they're spiteful and selfish enough that if they can't rule the world, they'll make sure nobody does. However, it <b><i>is</i></b> reasonable for somebody to believe that Solar or Lunar rule would be equally bad as the Realm, and want to try a <i><b>new</b></i> approach.<br /> <br /> The question is whether the Factions are monolithic and able to manipulate/deceive/mind-control/whatever their recruits into total ideological &quot;purity&quot;, or if there's room for differences of opinion and method within them. I would prefer the latter -- I don't know how the books currently present them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-30-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:19:52-07:00","id":683591,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's the other side of the typical image of the Curse-riddled Solars that makes no damn sense to me. &quot;Oh, our exagerated caricature of Desus is the poster boy for why the Usurpation happened!&quot; No he bloody isn't, you silly people. It's almost as bad as people thinking that Havesh represents some kind of return to the worst kinds of Solars, a guy who was murdered maybe six people ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T17:27:18-07:00","id":683650,"title":"","content":"I don't know what you mean by &quot;that&quot; Isator. Could you please be more specific?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T19:35:50-07:00","id":683757,"title":"","content":"I think his point is this (correct me if I'm wrong Isator):<br /> <br /> Desus was an arsehole, who beat and dominated his wife, punched out Oliphem's eye, and probably killed a few people.<br /> <br /> Bright Shattered Ice crea\u200bted a society where happy families were mandatory, and if you didn't make pleasant conversation with your family over the dinner table, you'd be murdered and replaced. Anyone who didn't seem happy enough generally, was murdered and replaced. She was probably responsible for the deaths of thousands.<br /> <br /> And there are still Solars who killed far, far more people, by pushing their mad whims on the populace.<br /> So Desus is an arsehole, \u200bwho is a Solar, but he is not at all why the Usurpation happened. If all the Solars were like him, the Sidereals wouldn't have bothered.<br /> <br /> It's like Mao. Mao didn't beat his wife or murder people for fun, but he had almost absolute power, so when he came up with a bad idea (the Great Leap Forward) colossal numbers of people died. When his power was threatened, to maintain power, thousands more were killed (I know a couple who were purged and sent to Heilongjiang, the northernmost province. She lived in a house with blood on the wall where people had been machine-gunned. He was forced to be a village doctor with no medical training, got chased by wolves, and nearly lost his feet to frostbite. All because Mao felt he was losing control of society.) Now, was he more evil than, say, a serial killer? Probably not. Did he do more harm than a serial killer? Vastly more, because of his incredible power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-30-2015, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T19:44:52-07:00","id":683764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683582#post683582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also important to realize how unsustainable it actually is to build a society that revolves entirely around an insatiable empire that will never be satisfied with zero annual growth, whose economy is by design dependent on rapaciously draining lives and wealth out of the finite Threshold (and systematically eviscerating the capacity of Threshold civilization to defend the borders of Creation, even while being demonstrably incapable of defending the borders in their place.) The Realm is inherently unstable and unsustainable, and puts Creation into a situation that will inevitably collapse. It's no different in this regard from any imperialist or growth-dependent regime in real history, with the added problem that destabilizing, depopulating, and un-developing the Threshold is a giant, neon-sign-waving invitation to another Balorian Crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div>We Brits did it for hundreds of years. That's why everyone here is speaking my language and not, say, Haudenensee. Although I don't think so, a lot of people (and not just in Britain) still think the British Empire was a good thing. I've met Africans who've said &quot;Oh, Britain was great because it taught us about Jesus&quot;, Chinese who've said &quot;Britain was great, look at how rich Hong Kong is compared to the mainland!&quot;, Arabs who've said &quot;You are from Britain? I love Britain! So much better than the corrupt officials we have now.&quot;<br /> <br /> For a less emotive example, think of Rome. Most people think Rome was great for Europe.<br /> <br /> So, I think it's legitimate for a lot of people to think that the Realm is a sensible thing.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say everyone will: I can definitely see a Sidereal who worries about the Solars but also dislikes the Realm. He'll either try working within the (Bronze) system, or hold his nose and work with the Solars for now, or find that he can't find many people to join him and be independent (there are probably some independents who don't care about politics, but others who definitely do, but don't like either of the current factions). I suspect most Sidereals will consider him na\u00efve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:14:50-07:00","id":683824,"title":"","content":"I get that Sidereals are cursed and arrogant, but I can't believe that all 100 of them, including the ones who are millennia old, are universally unable/unwilling to think more than a few centuries ahead, even after seeing what happened last time they only thought a few centuries ahead (the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade are what happened).<br /> <br /> We talk about it being dull and stereotypical to depict cursed Solars as always being &quot;Desus is an asshole who beat his wife and likes to hurt people.&quot; But then look at the Sidereals, and darnit if every last one of them isn't cursed with stereotypical &quot;Incapable of having a sensible idea or learning from my mistakes or planning for the future, hur hur so ironic, hurk-&quot; *<i>chokes on irony and dies</i>*<br /> <br /> It's very dull and one-note.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about Dune and Leto II and comparing him in my mind to Chejop Kejak, and I realized... Leto II is a monstrous, horrific person who does monstrous, horrific things, but he's compelling and even in a way admirable because he's competent enough to actually save humanity... and even the horrid things he did were part of a longer-term plan to teach humans to stop doing those same horrid things. Kejak wants to be Leto II, but is so effing incompetent that he fails miserably over and over again, and too narcissistic/stubborn/dumb/not-sure-what to admit he made any mistakes, so he keeps on robotically repeating the same thing over and over like he's already dead... it's not compelling, it's pathetic. Worse, it's patently obvious that all the monstrous, horrific things he's done have accomplished almost nothing, which makes him despicable.<br /> <br /> And the option for Sidereals who don't want to march along in lockstep is... join Team Solar Yay Nothing Can Possibly Go Wrong Here!, or become an independent and accept that your goals and plans for fate and Creation will have approximately 0 impact on anything that happens anywhere, ever, because the others hate you now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: If they only have two factions, then they're going to have varied beliefs and methods and disagreements within them, because people are people, they can think for themselves at least some of the time, and most Sidereals are too young to be <b><i>trapped</i></b> in the visions of th Great Prophecy the way Chejop Kejak is, to be unable to look beyond Option A and Option B. It's not really believable that everyone in each faction would agree on all things, and never be scheming against each other. There have got to be disagreements, quiet or open, and back-room deals between members of opposite factions, and Sidereals who do things against the dictates of their faction heads because they have a different idea of how &quot;rule by [Solars/Terrestrials]&quot; should be managed.<br /> <br /> And darnit, at least a few of them should have a plan that isn't pants-on-head idiotic once in a while.<br /> <br /> But this goes with my idea that Creation shouldn't be Doomed by default, and the PCs should not be obligated to be the Only Sane Ones who can save the world because <i><b>everybody</b></i> else everywhere is stoned and/or moronic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  clarifying what I meant: not that Sidereals should disagree with their faction heads but that its certain to me that some DO. 10-01-2015, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:33:07-07:00","id":683840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683824#post683824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But this goes with my idea that Creation shouldn't be Doomed by default, and the PCs should not be obligated to be the Only Sane Ones who can save the world because <i><b>everybody</b></i> else everywhere is stoned and/or moronic.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah but if the world isn't doomed and if everyone is too reasonable, where do we get awesome kung-fu fights and epic wars from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:44:07-07:00","id":683857,"title":"","content":"Disagreements between people who want different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T21:00:00-07:00","id":683886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683243#post683243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it's vastly easier to sell this after murdering everyone who actually remembers how much incomparably better most mortal quality of life and divine behavior were in the First Age. And then lying to the new recruits about how many Sidereals you murdered, what the First Age was like, and what the Great Prophecy actually said. And possibly making up some lies about how the Empress stopped the Great Contagion and &quot;of course&quot; nothing like that can ever happen again as long as she's in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Faction does not actually do any of this. Any of it. At all. They are not cartoonishly evil. Chejop Kejak and his inner circle are not actually running a long con on most of their brethren.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First Age was a time of singular wonders and the incredible peaks of sorcerous ingenuity among the god-kings that ruled the world unopposed.<br /> <br /> This may not necessarily have equated to a better life among mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The First Age not having been notably better than the Second Age for the populace sort of removes a lot of the baggage that makes the setting work and be interesting, in my view. The Age of Sorrows is supposed to be a fallen age not just for a few hundred god-kings, a few hundred &quot;in the entourage of the god-kings&quot;, and a few tens of thousands of &quot;not god-kings, but still pretty fucking elite.&quot; It's supposed to be a fallen age for <i>everyone</i>. The Exalted are important and have always ruled the world or at least most parts of it, but mortals count too; they aren't just background noise.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the Exalted come from human stock. Technically, they really should be referred to as &quot;Exalted humans.&quot; The Titanomachy wasn't just a power grab on the part of the Incarnae, it was also meant to uplift <i>all of humanity</i>. And it was supposed to have succeeded at that until it all went wrong.<br /> <br /> The First Age doesn't have to look like a magic inflected modern first world nation. (It probably <i>shouldn't</i> look like that.) It does probably have to be a lot better than the lot of mortals in the Age of Sorrows. Otherwise the Age of Sorrows isn't the Age of Sorrows, it's the Age of Pretty Much Like It's Always Been.<br /> <br /> That's a heck of a rallying cry for the Solars, isn't it? &quot;Go forth and reclaim the ancient glories! For yourselves. <i>Other people</i> don't matter and never have.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scarlet Dynasty is part of another reason why I was driven to find a more comprehensive image of what the Curse-addled Solars looked like, because I just don't see much credibility in the Sidereal Exalted being significantly concerned with mundane systems of oppression.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has always been a canonical part of the setting that <i>even the Gold Faction</i> finds the Vision of Bronze superior to what the Solars were going to turn into, if not what the Solars actually were at the tail end of the First Age. Now, to what extent the universe is still fulfilling the Vision of Bronze is debatable, but the Realm doesn't seem like it is significantly more oppressive than the Shogunate, which means that the Bronze Faction is still trying to minimize harm. The main point of contention between the two factions is &quot;The Vision of Gold is superior! It's a return to the grand days of the zenith of the First Age, when all worked as it should!&quot; and &quot;Yeah, <i>if you can pull it off</i>. You sound like a gambler saying all he needs to do is roll the hard eight and everything will great.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well sure, they're so isolated from humanity that they are unlikely to identify even remotely with mortals, or be at all concerned with what happens to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereals <i>are</i> humans. They're also humans who dedicate their entire life to protecting Creation. There are probably a number of them who don't give a shit about mortals, but as a group they care a great deal.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The worst of them committed horrible atrocities... but did not systematically reduce 99.99999% of humanity to grinding poverty with a huge side-helping of widespread chattel slavery. </div> </div> </div>The Realm doesn't do either of those things. Chattel slavery in the Realm exists and is a moral abomination, but is not widespread. The Realm is also not interested in reducing humanity to grinding, abject poverty. People in poverty are prone to do things like revolt, and they have trouble doing things like paying taxes. The Realm wants happy peasants. Happy peasants who know they're getting three full meals a day and have a snug warm house to sleep in and can afford a few simple luxuries and are reasonably certain they're not going to be arbitrarily abused by the powers that be, which accounts for most of the peasants in the Realm throughout its history, do NOT revolt. In fact they're likely to turn in rabble-rousers and malcontents rather than listen to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They also never did anything remotely as destructive as the Great Contagion, or it would have been mentioned in a book by now. So the entire notion that the Solars the biggest possible existential threat to humanity and Creation is already utterly absurd. </div> </div> </div>It's never been stated the Solars were the biggest possible existential threat to humanity and Creation. Indeed, the Solars, left unchecked in the First Age, would probably have tried very hard to sure that humanity survived... in a hellish dystopia.<br /> <br /> That said, it's entirely possible that First Age Solars could have eventually done something insane that destroyed the world. Those crazy motherfuckers weren't afraid to mess with reality on fundamental levels to satisfy their pet theories.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also important to realize how unsustainable it actually is to build a society that revolves entirely around an insatiable empire that will never be satisfied with zero annual growth, whose economy is by design dependent on rapaciously draining lives and wealth out of the finite Threshold (and systematically eviscerating the capacity of Threshold civilization to defend the borders of Creation, even while being demonstrably incapable of defending the borders in their place.) </div> </div> </div>This is just straight wrong. The Realm is not a parasite that kills its host. The Empress wasn't dumb and she managed her economy supremely well. Tribute from the Threshold is explicitly designed to not be more than Threshold states can bear, so that they can, in fact, continue to extract that tribute infinitely. If it weren't, places like An-Teng, which have been under the boot of the Realm for over half a millenium, would long since have dried up and blown away.<br /> <br /> The Realm is also demonstrably highly capable of defending the borders of Creation. The Realm has the Defense Grid. The Defense Grid is pretty fuckin' awesome at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Realm is inherently unstable and unsustainable, </div> </div> </div>The Realm has endured for seven and a half centuries with no serious external or internal threats. Its government has never fallen. It has never had a coup or a revolution or a military revolt. That is a track record which puts to shame every single real-world polity that has ever existed. The Empress was planning on being the Queen of Everything Forever and the system she developed was manifestly stable and sustainable over any sort of reasonably extended time horizon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with the added problem that destabilizing, depopulating, and un-developing the Threshold is a giant, neon-sign-waving invitation to another Balorian Crusade. </div> </div> </div>The Realm is doing none of those things to the Threshold with the possible exception of holding back development. The Realm does not destabilize; Realm satrapies that are well-governed, which is most of them, are some of the most stable places in Creation. The Realm might occasionally depopulate but never as a long-term plan; the Realm would prefer its satrapies to be filled with productive people doing productive things, because those people generate wealth that can be extracted. It might occasionally be necessary to make a mountain of skulls. That's a regrettable policy failure and not a long-term plan. Indeed, the population of the Threshold, over the past seven centuries, has massively<i> increased</i> under the stewardship of the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get that Sidereals are cursed and arrogant, but I can't believe that all 100 of them, including the ones who are millennia old, are universally unable/unwilling to think more than a few centuries ahead, even after seeing what happened last time they only thought a few centuries ahead (the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade are what happened). </div> </div> </div>The Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusade have jack and shit to do with the Sidereals lack of vision and foresight, they have to do with the fact that the Sidereals cannot see everything all the time and sometimes shit happens they have no control over. The Great Contagion was a one-off superweapon made by people outside of Fate that the Sidereals probably only had a vague idea were up to no good, and it enabled the Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> You <i>cannot plan for things like that</i>. You just can't. I'm sure the Sidereals have emergency contingency plans in place, but you can't devote resources to everything and &quot;every living thing in Creation sickens and dies from a plague even Charms have a hard time curing&quot; is one of those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Incapable of having a sensible idea or learning from my mistakes or planning for the future, hur hur so ironic, hurk-&quot; *<i>chokes on irony and dies</i>* </div> </div> </div>The Sidereals have many sensible ideas. Chejop and Ayesha are both sensible people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kejak wants to be Leto II, but is so effing incompetent that he fails miserably over and over again, and too narcissistic/stubborn/dumb/not-sure-what to admit he made any mistakes, so he keeps on robotically repeating the same thing over and over like he's already dead... it's not compelling, it's pathetic. </div> </div> </div>Chejop Kejak's career has been wildly successful. He implemented the Vision of Bronze; the Usurpation was a huge risk and he was instrumental in making it happen. After the First Age ended in a massive plague and Fair Folk invasion, he forged an alliance with the nascent Empress that has kept the world mostly stable and mostly intact as it slowly claws its way back out from under that particular apocalypse. He's had failures, but has learned and adapted from them.<br /> <br /> He is not a miserable failure.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or become an independent and accept that your goals and plans for fate and Creation will have approximately 0 impact on anything that happens anywhere, ever, because the others hate you now. </div> </div> </div>Nazri is the Chair of the Convention of Fire. His goals and plans for Fate and Creation have quite a lot of impact on things across an entire Direction. He is an independent.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and darnit, at least a few of them should have a plan that isn't pants-on-head idiotic once in a while. </div> </div> </div>Neither the plans of the Bronze nor the Gold Faction are particular idiotic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 10-01-2015, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T21:00:26-07:00","id":683887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683824#post683824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We talk about it being dull and stereotypical to depict cursed Solars as always being &quot;Desus is an asshole who beat his wife and likes to hurt people.&quot; But then look at the Sidereals, and darnit if every last one of them isn't cursed with stereotypical &quot;Incapable of having a sensible idea or learning from my mistakes or planning for the future, hur hur so ironic, hurk-&quot; *<i>chokes on irony and dies</i>*<br /> <br /> It's very dull and one-note.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about Dune and Leto II and comparing him in my mind to Chejop Kejak, and I realized... Leto II is a monstrous, horrific person who does monstrous, horrific things, but he's compelling and even in a way admirable because he's competent enough to actually save humanity... and even the horrid things he did were part of a longer-term plan to teach humans to stop doing those same horrid things. Kejak wants to be Leto II, but is so effing incompetent that he fails miserably over and over again, and too narcissistic/stubborn/dumb/not-sure-what to admit he made any mistakes, so he keeps on robotically repeating the same thing over and over like he's already dead... it's not compelling, it's pathetic. Worse, it's patently obvious that all the monstrous, horrific things he's done have accomplished almost nothing, which makes him despicable.<br /> <br /> And the option for Sidereals who don't want to march along in lockstep is... join Team Solar Yay Nothing Can Possibly Go Wrong Here!, or become an independent and accept that your goals and plans for fate and Creation will have approximately 0 impact on anything that happens anywhere, ever, because the others hate you now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If they're going to have only two factions, at least those factions ought to have varied beliefs and methods and disagreements within them, and darnit, at least a few of them should have a plan that isn't pants-on-head idiotic once in a while.<br /> <br /> But this goes with my idea that Creation shouldn't be Doomed by default, and the PCs should not be obligated to be the Only Sane Ones who can save the world because <i><b>everybody</b></i> else everywhere is stoned and/or moronic.<br /> <br /> It's also not really believable that everyone in each faction would agree on all things, and not be scheming against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do broadly agree with you.<br /> <br /> But there are a couple of points. First, to be fair, Chejop <i>has</i>, so far, saved Creation. The Solars didn't destroy the world. The Deathlords didn't destroy the world. The Raska didn't destroy the world. The Lunars haven't even managed to destroy the Realm.<br /> <br /> The issue though, is this is largely portrayed as not much to do with Chejop. The Empress saved the world, with Chejop just helping a little. Before that, the contagion failed because of the Raksha. If, say, Chejop had gone &quot;there's one way to save Creation... we need to provoke the Raksha to invade. It's a hard and desperate choice, but we need to do it to save Creation&quot; or something like that. Followed by him perhaps showing the Empress how to get into the Imperial Manse, or something.<br /> <br /> The other thing, of course, is that Creation is basically presented as being doomed. So, although in fact Chejop's plan does seem to have worked, you're basically told &quot;it's about to fail unless someone else saves the day&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also make a point about the Gold Faction, which you described as Team Solar Yay Nothing Can Possibly Go Wrong Here! Now, if you read Cult of the Illuminated, that is how Ayesha Ura is. But Lupo, her second-in-command, does actually remember the first age, and knows that it absolutely could go wrong. That's why he has a different way of training Solars, and a different view of them, because he wants to make sure that this time it'll go right. So it's not like everyone in the Cult is a blind idiot.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T21:03:20-07:00","id":683891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683857#post683857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagreements between people who want different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>which won't be solved by Eclipse super-diplomacy and keen organizational/logistical acumen how? because the way that some people talk about it, you'd think the game was some sort of anthropological dissertation about how society works or something, and that all the fighting is worse than useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T21:50:21-07:00","id":683934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683824#post683824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that Sidereals are cursed and arrogant, but <b>I can't believe that all 100 of them, including the ones who are millennia old, are universally unable/unwilling to think more than a few centuries ahead\u2026</b></div> </div> </div> </div>When's the last time <i>you</i> did?<br /> <br /> &quot;The future&quot; is a pretty abstract subject in the human mind; I'd think that even with a five thousand year lifespan, most Sidereal plots culminate in years or maybe decades, as opposed to centuries or millennia. It's just too outside the human wheelhouse to be a common thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T22:10:57-07:00","id":683944,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it's the Sidereal's job to plan out the future and think about what kind of extremely long-term consequences and ramifications some act might have. That's like kind of, their entire schtick as weavers of Fate, to be the ones planning and contemplating what will happen in the distant future. So I can see why some people are unhappy that they often come across as rather myopic in the gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T03:02:53-07:00","id":684165,"title":"","content":"Planning centuries ahead is difficult, because a lot of things can happen in the course of centuries that throw all of your plans off.<br /> <br /> Planning a few <i>months</i> ahead is difficult for much the same reason.<br /> <br /> It's good to have plans, but contrary to what some kinds of anime would have you believe, the best planners are the ones who make plans that can accommodate all of the ways reality won't live up to the plan, rather than come up with that one absolutely flawless plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:06:17-07:00","id":684237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684165#post684165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's good to have plans, but contrary to what some kinds of anime would have you believe, the best planners are the ones who make plans that can accommodate all of the ways reality won't live up to the plan, rather than come up with that one absolutely flawless plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>My company has been doing essentially the same thing since it was founded. We have addressed hundreds of problems with our platform. It isn't even that sophisticated, when you get right down to it. Bugs, conflicts, unexpected user actions, etc, are all addressed and handled. And yet, every time we squash a problem, another one comes up.<br /> <br /> Entropy is a thing. and it eats &quot;flawless&quot; anything, given time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:14:27-07:00","id":684243,"title":"","content":"Still, I've been forming some new ideas about how the whole Fate and Destiny thing might work, which I think manage to be comprehensive at the same time as elegantly simple. I might elaborate on them a bit later.<br /> <br /> All I'll say at the moment is that they emerge from the starting premise of how there might be an ideal person out there for one to be with, and circumstance might even afford one the unlikely opportunity to be with them by virtue of a potential encounter, and then it never happens because mild happenstance or one's own personality or decisions mean you never quite get to speaking to them, and the chance is lost forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T05:33:26-07:00","id":684299,"title":"","content":"In mid-September I put in a request at work to use my vacation time to have Samhain's Eve off, and started planning a gaming session for it; I invited players, made arrangements for folks living two hundred miles away to stay the night, even discussed with family the possibility of costume themes and inventive dinner ideas.<br /> <br /> Then today I was told that no one would be able to cover my shift that night and I'd have to come in and work.<br /> <br /> Until I can see a month-and-a-half plan of mine hold together, I refuse to believe that Sidereals should be expected to cover every eventuality when planning for the next thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T05:56:57-07:00","id":684336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683887#post683887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd also make a point about the Gold Faction, which you described as Team Solar Yay Nothing Can Possibly Go Wrong Here! Now, if you read Cult of the Illuminated, that is how Ayesha Ura is. But Lupo, her second-in-command, does actually remember the first age, and knows that it absolutely could go wrong. That's why he has a different way of training Solars, and a different view of them, because he wants to make sure that this time it'll go right. So it's not like everyone in the Cult is a blind idiot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Lupo is best Sidereal. I hope to make a Sidereal just like him:<br /> &quot;You may be the hero returning to make everything better, I might be helping you- but don't think for a SECOND that I won't be doing everything I can to put you on the grinder, to keep you in line, to teach you responsibility and discipline. If I have to the one to make sure you don't turn out like the people that ruled the First Age, so be it, if I have to be harsh on you, so be it. But dammit, I will do it and things will be better.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:12:38-07:00","id":684352,"title":"","content":"I found him to not only to be the most sensible Sidereal in the Gold Faction, but I also found his training camp (Kether Rock) to be far more interesting* than the Sequestered Tabernacle, Ayesha's project. Though, this is not to say they don't have a place, in order to come out with Solar NPCs who are just breathtakingly arrogant. Though putting it close to the most powerful canon circle of Solars (ie the Bull and Samea) seemed a little foolish (and then there's the issue of how the camps are written as if about half of Solars are in Cult camps, but that's a different issue).<br /> <br /> *And, luckily, that's the one in the direction in which my game's set, which is important since 2 of the PCs are members of the Cult.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:26:37-07:00","id":684359,"title":"","content":"Part of my ideas for how Destiny works do have the idea that during the First Age there were various factors, such as the management of the world and its ontological issues by the Exalted, the relative restraint of the Celestial gods, operating budgets that were a lot higher (you had billions of people and a lot of holidays sending constant streams of Essence and cash in huge quantities to Heaven) and the Sidereals being aided by all kinds of wondrous tools they could get the Realm to produce for them, it was a lot easier both to make plans for unfolding history that could be adhered to a lot more smoothly, and kind of make the world... nicer. People would still have to put some of their own work in, but the world could be a bit less arbitrary about some things, so people who were really ideal for each other didn't need to have their happiness prevented by little things like being on opposite sides of the world from one another.<br /> <br /> When I say tools made by Solars, I'm thinking of things like thinking automatons optimised to helping manage the unintuitive workload of destiny management, engines capable of modelling all kinds of life intersections and alternate futures, and even things like writing kits made to allow Sidereals to write out all of the necessary orders and directives to precisely manage enormous numbers of destinies per day in a manner that transcended the physical limits of how much paperwork a human shaped thing can do in that time. Not things that replaced the powers of Sidereals, but complemented them; the kinds of tools that would be useful to somebody with World-Shaping Artistic Vision in a similar way to how a daiklave is useful to somebody with Hungry Tiger Technique.<br /> <br /> I don't see Chejop Kejak as having been a very sentimental man even in the First Age (I've got this image in which Chejop has incidentally had numerous children over the centuries, and isn't very interested in any of them beyond doing a bit to give them destinies to insulate them from some arbitrary disasters; I don't see this as necessarily being a flaw), but I can imagine some old Sidereals who occasionally look at the work they have to do now (not in terms of &quot;we must make Hard Choices for the Greater Good&quot; so much as it just being a bit... grubbier), and look back with nostalgia on the times when being an agent of Fate meant you did a more meaningful equivalent of ensuring that it never rained unless everybody had an umbrella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T07:31:58-07:00","id":684401,"title":"","content":"So, Mercushio, I may be misunderstanding your post but you appear to be saying that the majority of humans in Creation <i><b>don't</b></i> live in poverty? Let's see... they live in a world of constant warfare where warfare is apparently necessary just to find enough to eat, nobody has access to clean water and most don't have a reliable food supply either (hence the disease and warfare), they live in mud huts or wooden shacks or at best small urban hovels, most roads aren't paved if they exist at all, starvation and disease are rampant and uncontrolled, chattel slavery is all over, the weather is totally out of control.... everywhere in the entire Threshold. Not to mention the Fair Folk, Wyld mutants, and undead marauding everywhere and killing people constantly. The only humans who are slightly better off are the wealthy, who are a vanishingly tiny minority and still don't have clean water or peace. You don't consider that to be a low standard of living?<br /> <br /> Your post also looks like you're saying that the extractive empire set up by the Empress does <i><b>none</b></i> of the things that absolutely every single extractive empire in all of human history has done to every nation they conquered.<br /> <br /> You seem to have a very rosy, idyllic view of empires in which everybody is happy and healthy and exploitation never causes any actual harm, either at home or in the conquered countries. (You also seem to say the Isle and Satrapies never had any rebellions, which is not what the books say.) I don't think you realize how structurally destructive empires inherently are to the conquered societies. The &quot;order&quot; they impose is solely the order of external hierarchical obedience (because anyone who disobeys is killed). Everything else is systematically chopped apart. The society and culture and civilization conquered and subjugated to extract material wealth and human slaves inevitably crumbles into poverty and dysfunction -- this has been demonstrated, historically, in every single empire for which we have any historical data. Look at the Third World today -- those countries didn't start out dysfunctional and broken since the dawn of humanity. That chaos is the result of centuries of slave trade and extractive imperialism, which destroyed the cultural institutions that once existed and plunged formerly prosperous countries into poverty and chaos. Now imagine that everywhere there isn't a stable government, everywhere that disease or war temporarily wipes out a big chunk of the population (such as the recent Ebola epidemic) the Wyld or undead can move in and take over permanently.<br /> <br /> I have also read explicit statements -- I think by authors and devs on this forum -- that every time a civilization independent of the Realm becomes large or prosperous or unified out in the outer Threshold, the Legions go and utterly raze it to the ground because it's a rival and might be infeseted with Lunars. This probably means only polities that are getting <i><b>quite</b></i> large and independent, since they haven't wiped out Halta, for example.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empire is also very foolishly and short-sightedly designed to depend utterly on the immortality of a being who cannot possibly be immortal because no Exalt is immortal, and everybody has known this since the Thousand Struggles Era. And Oh Look! as soon as she <i><b>inevitably</b></i> went away her supposed &quot;orderly utopia&quot; immediately collapsed. That is not a sustainable society even internally, even ignoring the way the empire is designed to eviscerate human society in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> And Sidereals live long enough to witness the decay firsthand, and realize what is happening, in a way that mortals and even Dragon-Blooded cannot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The problems with the Visions of Bronze and Gold started from the moment the Great Prophecy was cast. Every Sidereal present assumed three facts that were utterly false:<br /> <br /> 1. The Bronze and Gold are the only possible solutions that can ever or will ever exist, therefore we should never attempt to have any other ideas.<br /> 2. This Prophecy accounts for all the known and unknown threats from outside of Fate, and therefore we can trust the Visions to be 100% accurate and trustworthy.<br /> 3. If either Bronze or Gold Vision succeeds, it will have succeeded <i><b>for all eternity</b></i>, because we can see infinitely far into the future. Neither Vision will ever come to an end in all of eternity, or require a new prophecy, let alone a new Vision.<br /> <br /> Every Sidereal should have known better than 2 (which is contrary to the known laws of Fate) and 3 (which is contrary to the existence of Endings) but from the very start, they failed to realize this. And in all the time they've been watching Creation disintegrate, the faction elders still haven't guessed that 1, 2, and 3 are not true. Due apparently to the Great Curse, they took leave of logic and sense, and the elders who are still alive are <i><b>stuck that way</b></i>.<br /> <br /> It's pretty obvious to me, for example, that the Vision of Bronze only actually predicted the course of things until the Great Contagion and that it no longer has any relevance to what's happened in Creation since then. The Bronze Faction is currently flying blind, on utterly outdated and irrelevant information.<br /> <br /> (To Mercushio, I simply disagree with your opinion that the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade were not failures because a small, crumbling, very doomed remnant of Creation still exists for now, but we'll have to agree to disagree there.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I think that the younger Sidereals, who are not chained to the Great Prophecy because they weren't there, would notice that 2 and 3 are BS and 1 is looking mighty dodgy as well. Most are probably smart enough to notice that the current state of Creation is bad and getting worse, and that repeating the same old plans is not working. They would not blindly obey Chejop and Ayesha and agree with everything the leaders tell them. There are going to be disagreements because they are going to notice how often their leaders' plans are out of touch with reality.<br /> <br /> I think there must be a lot of younger Sidereals who agree only loosely with the broad thrust of one of the factions, but have their own very different goals for how to carry them out because they disagree with their leaders. There are young Sidereals who only pretend to belong to a faction, who are actually independents who quietly discuss among themselves what Third Option would be best. There might be a few independents who really don't have any opinion about what to do, but most of them are likely to care enough to have their own idea about what should be done. I think very few of the younger Sidereals, possibly none of them, are so blinded by the Curse that they think the current plans are working perfectly and requires no changes.<br /> <br /> And by &quot;young&quot; Sidereals, I include those who were born during the Shogunate and witnessed the Great Contagion, too. I mean pretty much everyone younger than Ayesha Ura. I think the majority of Sidereals have ideas of their own and do not agree with every single thing their leaders tell them to believe and do. They are arrogant and often callous, but most aren't stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-01-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T07:38:40-07:00","id":684426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684401#post684401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problems with the Visions of Bronze and Gold started from the moment the Great Prophecy was cast. Every Sidereal present assumed three facts that were utterly false:<br /> <br /> 1. The Bronze and Gold are the only possible solutions that can ever or will ever exist, therefore we should never attempt to have any other ideas.<br /> 2. This Prophecy accounts for all the known and unknown threats from outside of Fate, and therefore we can trust the Visions to be 100% accurate and trustworthy.<br /> 3. If either Bronze or Gold Vision succeeds, it will have succeeded <i><b>for all eternity</b></i>, because we can see infinitely far into the future. Neither Vision will ever come to an end in all of eternity, or require a new prophecy, let alone a new Vision.<br /> <br /> Every Sidereal should have known better than 2 (which is contrary to the known laws of Fate) and 3 (which is contrary to the existence of Endings) but from the very start, they failed to realize this. And in all the time they've been watching Creation disintegrate, the faction elders still haven't guessed that 1, 2, and 3 are not true. Due apparently to the Great Curse, they took leave of logic and sense, and the elders who are still alive are <i><b>stuck that way</b></i>.<br /> <br /> It's pretty obvious to me, for example, that the Vision of Bronze only actually predicted the course of things until the Great Contagion and that it no longer has any relevance to what's happened in Creation since then. The Bronze Faction is currently flying blind, on utterly outdated and irrelevant information.</div> </div> </div> </div>At times like this, I really feel for Coik.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T07:45:27-07:00","id":684430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=683891#post683891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which won't be solved by Eclipse super-diplomacy and keen organizational/logistical acumen how?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even the Solars can create a permanent utopia. Not even the keenest diplomats can force compromise between people that refuse to sit at the same table, absent some contextual thing that gets them there. <br /> <br /> This is part of the problem with past editions imagining (and implementing) Solar social charms as perfect-brainwash-lasers. It's overpowered but more than that, it's boring and takes away from the personal drama of deal-brokering in favor of &quot;magic is an actor, and fixes everything on its own.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:32:46-07:00","id":684478,"title":"","content":"*long slurp of tea*<br /> <br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684401#post684401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problems with the Visions of Bronze and Gold started from the moment the Great Prophecy was cast. Every Sidereal present assumed three facts that were utterly false:<br /> <br /> 1. The Bronze and Gold are the only possible solutions that can ever or will ever exist, therefore we should never attempt to have any other ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assertion fundamentally misunderstands the Great Prophecy. The Great Prophecy was not Kejak and friends shaking a Magic Eight Ball and getting three fortune cookies spat out. The Great Prophecy was a thousand thousand prophecies, cast by the entire Fivescore Fellowship, to the furthest reaches of the Loom (remember this was written when most Sidereal prophecy Charms required at least three Sidereals of different castes to work, and were more effective the more Sidereals present. Even that presupposes that the best way to mechanically represent the Great Prophecy is through Charms, or that it should be mechanically representatable at all)<br /> <br /> If anything, the three Visions are amaglamations of hundreds or thousands of visions that follow the same theme; the Vision of Gold in particular is called out as having taken the longest to form because the smaller prophecies that would eventually comprise it were so varied that it took the Sidereals a while to see any commonality between them. Hell, you could make a decent argument either way that the Visions are distinct things that exist in setting and that the Visions are constructs for us, to players, to sum up the Great Prophecy without it having to be mindmeltingly complex or the length of an entire fucking fatsplat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. This Prophecy accounts for all the known and unknown threats from outside of Fate, and therefore we can trust the Visions to be 100% accurate and trustworthy. </div> </div> </div>This is based on shit writing that puts the Sidereals' heads so far up their own ass that they can see out their throats, particularly impressive because it comes from a one-two punch of what's written about Fate and what's written about the Sidereal Curse. Putting aside that the Outside Fate mechanics don't even remotely match up with the commentary, it presumes such monumental arrogance and stupidity on the part of the Sidereals that it goes beyond &quot;tragic flaw&quot; into &quot;grotesque parody.&quot; To the point where it's not even appropiate for T-Rexs in F-14s Exalted.<br /> <br /> Now, I can see where you're coming from...I'm usually the first person in line bitching about how Sidereals are portrayed as monumental idiots who put their hats on their feet and shoes on their hands. But it's important to remember that it's a problem with <i>portrayal</i> and not supposed to be taken as how Sidereals actually are in setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. If either Bronze or Gold Vision succeeds, it will have succeeded <i><b>for all eternity</b></i>, because we can see infinitely far into the future. Neither Vision will ever come to an end in all of eternity, or require a new prophecy, let alone a new Vision. </div> </div> </div>...do I even need to address this one?<br /> <br /> Okay. I'll just say: Both Chejop Kejak and Ayesha Ura are smart enough to have heard of and then comprehended the phrase &quot;No plan survives contact with the enemy.&quot; And considering that I am not a fan of Ayesha Ura and have heavily criticized her in the past...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684426#post684426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At times like this, I really feel for Coik.</div> </div> </div> </div>:*<br /> <br /> Since this thread started with Sidereal politics, <a href=\"http://www.doctorshrugs.com/foxhound/comic.php?id=300\" target=\"_blank\">here's</a> Psycho Mantis and Revolver Ocelot discussing them. I'd post the most relevant section but Imageshack seems to be having issues at the moment...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","user":"Coik","date":". 10-01-2015, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:40:46-07:00","id":684493,"title":"","content":"You guys, I just got through reading a series of <i>Calvin and Hobbes</i> anthologies.<br /> <br /> <i>It's Tyrannosaurs in F-<b>14s</b>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:42:59-07:00","id":684495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684359#post684359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of my ideas for how Destiny works do have the idea that during the First Age there were various factors, such as the management of the world and its ontological issues by the Exalted, the relative restraint of the Celestial gods, operating budgets that were a lot higher (you had billions of people and a lot of holidays sending constant streams of Essence and cash in huge quantities to Heaven) and the Sidereals being aided by all kinds of wondrous tools they could get the Realm to produce for them, it was a lot easier both to make plans for unfolding history that could be adhered to a lot more smoothly, and kind of make the world... nicer. People would still have to put some of their own work in, but the world could be a bit less arbitrary about some things, so people who were really ideal for each other didn't need to have their happiness prevented by little things like being on opposite sides of the world from one another.<br /> <br /> When I say tools made by Solars, I'm thinking of things like thinking automatons optimised to helping manage the unintuitive workload of destiny management, engines capable of modelling all kinds of life intersections and alternate futures, and even things like writing kits made to allow Sidereals to write out all of the necessary orders and directives to precisely manage enormous numbers of destinies per day in a manner that transcended the physical limits of how much paperwork a human shaped thing can do in that time. Not things that replaced the powers of Sidereals, but complemented them; the kinds of tools that would be useful to somebody with World-Shaping Artistic Vision in a similar way to how a daiklave is useful to somebody with Hungry Tiger Technique.<br /> <br /> I don't see Chejop Kejak as having been a very sentimental man even in the First Age (I've got this image in which Chejop has incidentally had numerous children over the centuries, and isn't very interested in any of them beyond doing a bit to give them destinies to insulate them from some arbitrary disasters; I don't see this as necessarily being a flaw), but I can imagine some old Sidereals who occasionally look at the work they have to do now (not in terms of &quot;we must make Hard Choices for the Greater Good&quot; so much as it just being a bit... grubbier), and look back with nostalgia on the times when being an agent of Fate meant you did a more meaningful equivalent of ensuring that it never rained unless everybody had an umbrella.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had something relating to this thought as well...with some extra stuff rolled in to boot.<br /> <br /> We know that the Solars and Lunars were awesome at securing the borders of the Wyld. Massive Terraforming engines rolled out to make new Creation for people to live in, and the combined operation of those, the Order-conferring Trade Pattern, the large populations, and the Order-generating Obelisks meant that Wyld Incursions were few and far between. High-end Solar Sorcerers can stroll in and slap the undo button on a Shadowland, and the Deathlords didn't exist yet. These things combined mean that there was a lot less Outside-Fate intervention to deal with. This means that when Fate was laid out, it tended to not get screwed up by something they couldn't see coming.<br /> <br /> In addition, the Sidereals operated more openly...no Arcane Fate. They cooperated with the rest of the Exalted to seek the best of the world. As it is now, if there is a demon-summoning cult that the Siddies see messing with their plans, they either have to manipulate up a Wyld Hunt, or they have to deal with it themselves. In the First Age, they could send a note to the office of whichever Solar ruled over those lands, informing him that he had a Yozi-cult infestation, and information on where to find it. The Solar himself may not even see the memo, but it would move through the bureaucracy (that was actually efficient, because Solars were running it) and make it back to the Dragonblooded manager of that particular territory, and he'd send troops out to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Really...in the First Age, the Sidereals largely operated as advisers and planners. If the Solars had an idea that they wanted to Fate-check, they called up a few Sidereals and had them cast prophecies to see how it would go. If a Lunar was hunting a Wyld Incursion, they could just Infallible Messenger a Siddie and say 'Hey, could you look for Fate disruptions in this general area? I'm trying to locate where they are coming out of the Wyld.' Yeah, they'd still go do field work...some stuff needs the touch of a Chosen of Fate...but they were much less overworked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:47:33-07:00","id":684497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684493#post684493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys, I just got through reading a series of <i>Calvin and Hobbes</i> anthologies.<br /> <br /> <i>It's Tyrannosaurs in F-<b>14s</b>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Noted and corrected. My misrembering of Calvin and Hobbes lore fills with me shame.<br /> <br /> I will now listen to five Keh-dollar sign-ha songs as penance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:47:49-07:00","id":684498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684401#post684401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Mercushio, you'r3 saying that the majority of humans in Creation <i><b>don't</b></i> live in poverty?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking about Creation or are we talking about the Realm and its satrapies? Those sets do not completely overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's see... they live in a world of constant warfare where warfare is apparently necessary just to find enough to eat, nobody has access to clean water and most don't have a reliable food supply either (hence the disease and warfare), </div> </div> </div>The Realm is not subject to constant warfare. Indeed, the Blessed Isle has been free of war for over seven centuries.<br /> <br /> Nor, in fact, is Creation. Many parts of it go many generations without seeing war.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of people who have access to clean water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they live in mud huts or wooden shacks or at best small urban hovels, most roads aren't paved if they exist at all, starvation and disease are rampant and uncontrolled, chattel slavery is all over, the weather is totally out of control.... everywhere in the entire Threshold. </div> </div> </div><i>This is explicitly not true.</i><br /> <br /> Starvation and disease are not for the most part rampant and uncontrolled in the Threshold, because the Threshold is ruled by the Realm and the Realm in fact does a pretty good job keeping those things under control, because satraps answer to their Great House and to the Empress, and the Great Houses and the Empress ask pointed question if all your peasants get sick and die and aren't paying taxes or extracting resources anymore. The weather is not totally out of control anywhere in Creation, and it is especially not out of control in the Realm proper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention the Fair Folk, Wyld mutants, and undead marauding everywhere and killing people constantly. </div> </div> </div>The Realm does a really, really good job of keeping those things out of their satrapies. That's what the Legions are for. That's what the Wyld Hunt is for. Does it happen? Sure, especially in satrapies bordering Lunar dominions. It is not happening &quot;constantly.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only humans who are slightly better off are the wealthy, who are a vanishingly tiny minority and still don't have clean water or peace. </div> </div> </div>In the Realm, yes they do. Being a wealthy person in the Realm is pretty fucking sweet. You do get clean water and peace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't consider that to be a low standard of living? </div> </div> </div>I would if you were right about anything you just said.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're also saying that the extractive empire set up by the Empress does <i><b>none</b></i> of the things that absolutely every single extractive empire in all of human history has done to every nation they conquered. </div> </div> </div>The Realm was put together and then ruled by an immortal Empress with the keys to a globe-shattering superweapon who was planning on living forever. Her priorities and method of rule are going to be executed somewhat differently in some ways than those of real-world equivalent empires, of which there are none, because every real-world equivalent you could possibly analogize to the Realm fell completely apart in a fraction of the time the Realm has endured.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to have a very rosy, idyllic view of empires in which everybody is happy and healthy and exploitation never causes any actual harm, </div> </div> </div>I have no such view and you cannot find a single quote or statement in which I express said view. The Realm causes immense harm to millions of people. It's going to dictate how and when you worship. It's going to actively prevent your nation from developing advanced industry and focus it instead towards resource extraction and cash crops. You will be ruled by someone who was born half a world away, across the inland sea, who has turned the governing apparatus of your nation into a puppet show. They will defend you, but they will also remove any ability you have to defend yourself. Their tax structure will be explicitly designed not to kill you, but to make it really hard for you to amass wealth and power. Trying to change any of that is a real great way to end up with your head on pike.<br /> <br /> What they're <i>not going</i> to do is suck your country dry and let it blow away. The harm they cause is different than that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (You also seem to say the Isle and Satrapies never had any rebellions, which is not what the books say.) </div> </div> </div>I said no such thing. I said that the Realm hasn't had a real threat to its system of government and leader, which is unambiguously true. Stuff like the Unbroken Rushes Rebellion never got anywhere near toppling the Empress or being more than a footnote in Realm history, and satrapy rebellions end with pacified satrapies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think you realize how structurally destructive empires inherently are to the conquered societies. The &quot;order&quot; they impose is solely the order of external hierarchical obedience (because anyone who disobeys is killed). Everything else is systematically chopped apart. The society and culture and civilization conquered and subjugated to extract material wealth and human slaves inevitably crumbles </div> </div> </div>An-Teng and Chiaroscuro have been ruled by the Realm, directly in one case and indirectly in another, for over half a millennium. They show no signs of instability (indeed, An-Teng is the jewel in the crown of the Realm's colonial empire) and are doing better now than they've ever done before.<br /> <br /> That's twenty-five human generations of stability, order, and prosperity. Any polity that managed that in the real world would go down in history as one of the stablest, best-run empires of all time.<br /> <br /> You keep using the word &quot;inevitable.&quot; Every system of government has a failure state. The Realm's seems to be remarkably stable and effective. The books <i>present the Realm</i> as remarkably stable and effective. It wasn't about to tumble! It wasn't growing progressively more unstable! It was going great!<br /> <br /> You can argue that this is unrealistic, but you cannot argue that the Realm was a rotten edifice, because it <i>wasn't.</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now imagine that everywhere there isn't a stable government, everywhere that disease or war temporarily wipes out a big chunk of the population (such as the recent Ebola epidemic) the Wyld or undead get to move in and take over permanently. </div> </div> </div>... that's not what happens in Creation where disease or war wipe out a big chunk of the population. If it were, there would be no Creation left, because that precise thing has happened a lot of times in a lot of places in Creation.<br /> <br /> It can happen. You speak as if it is a foregone conclusion. It isn't. Sometimes a mass death even causes a shadowland to emerge. Sometimes it just means the land is reduced to howling wilderness until it is resettled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Scarlet Empire is also very foolishly and short-sightedly designed to depend utterly on the immortality of a being who cannot possibly be immortal because no Exalt is immortal </div> </div> </div>,<br /> <br /> You can become immortal in Creation through the use of a <i>Hearthstone</i>, of all things. You think Scarlet didn't have a reasonable plan for not dying?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and everybody has known this since the Thousand Struggles Era. And Oh Look! as soon as she <i><b>inevitably</b></i> went away her supposed &quot;orderly utopia&quot; immediately collapsed. </div> </div> </div>Scarlet never presented the Realm as a utopia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is not a sustainable society even internally, even ignoring the way the empire is designed to eviscerate human society in the Threshold. </div> </div> </div>It was stable for seven and a half centuries. It beats every single real world polity that has ever existed for stability and longevity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Sidereals live long enough to witness the decay firsthand, and realize what is happening, in a way that mortals and even Dragon-Blooded cannot. </div> </div> </div><i>What decay?</i> The Realm wasn't decaying!<br /> <br /> You have a conception of what you think the Realm should be that is massively and fundamentally at odds with the Realm as it is actually written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problems with the Visions of Bronze and Gold started from the moment the Great Prophecy was cast. Every Sidereal present assumed three facts that were utterly false:<br /> <br /> 1. The Bronze and Gold are the only possible solutions that can ever or will ever exist, therefore we should never attempt to have any other ideas.<br /> 2. This Prophecy accounts for all the known and unknown threats from outside of Fate, and therefore we can trust the Visions to be 100% accurate and trustworthy.<br /> 3. If either Bronze or Gold Vision succeeds, it will have succeeded <i><b>for all eternity</b></i>, because we can see infinitely far into the future. Neither Vision will ever come to an end in all of eternity, or require a new prophecy, let alone a new Vision. </div> </div> </div>Number one is actually true, as long as you're operating within Fate. The Sidereals were indeed short-sighted to not realize you could go outside of Fate, but at that point you're going crazy off the map. They don't actually control resources outside of Fate, at that point you're down to things like &quot;try and manipulate the Yozis or the Neverborn or the shinma to get results we can't get otherwise.&quot; It is somewhat understandable they didn't want to try that.<br /> <br /> No Sidereal, ever, has ever assumed that the Great Prophecy accounted for unknown threats outside of Fate, or that they could trust the Visions to be 100% accurate and trustworthy. You cannot find anything in the text to support either assertion.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals did assume that the greatest and most accurate prophecy they ever put together was, in fact, mostly accurate and trustworthy. The Visions are not written, by the writers, to be unreliable bullshit; they were written to be actual-factual things that gave the Sidereals good information. You have not discovered some super secret of the setting, that the Sidereals are actually idiots in this regard.<br /> <br /> The continued validity of the Visions is indeed somewhat up in the air, but I don't think the Sidereals themselves would actually deny that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's pretty obvious to me, for example, that the Vision of Bronze only actually predicted the course of things until the Great Contagion and that it no longer has any relevance to what's happened in Creation since then. The Bronze Faction is currently flying blind, on utterly outdated and irrelevant information. </div> </div> </div>You just made a very strong anti-Bronze Faction argument, one that is likely mirrored in-setting by other Sidereals.<br /> <br /> The Bronze response to that would be &quot;We could try and build something better than the Realm, but that's an incredibly high-risk endeavor. We don't consider the risk worth the reward; what if we fail?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not a crazy response. The Bronze Faction isn't written to be crazy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (To Mercushio, I simply disagree with your opinion that the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade were not failures because a tiny, crumbling fraction of Creation still exists (<i><b>very</b></i> temporarily), but I'll leave it at that.) </div> </div> </div>... the Balorian Crusade and the Great Contagion weren't not failures on the part of the Sidereals because the vast bulk of Creation still exists and doesn't seem to be going anywhere anytime soon. They weren't failures on their part because they were <i>unforseeable events.</i><br /> <br /> Blaming that on them would be like my blaming the U.S government for Cthulhu crawling out of the ocean, or for a zombie apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think that the younger Sidereals, who are not chained to the Great Prophecy because they weren't there, would notice that 2 and 3 are BS and 1 is looking mighty dodgy as well. </div> </div> </div>Which do you consider more likely, that the younger Sidereals are that dumb and haven't noticed, or that there is, in fact, nothing to notice?<br /> <br /> Again, you seem to be conflating how you think the setting should work with how the setting is actually written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most are probably smart enough to notice that the current state of Creation is bad and getting worse, and that repeating the same old plans is not working. </div> </div> </div>Most of the people noticing that are likely to give the Gold Faction, as the revolutionary upstarts who have a new plan that upends the status quo, a serious hearing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They would not blindly obey Chejop and Ayesha like mindless little robots, because most of them aren't idiots. There are going to be disagreements because they are going to notice how often their leaders' plans are out of touch with reality. </div> </div> </div>Neither Chejop nor Ayesha are written as being out of touch with reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there are going to be a lot of younger Sidereals who agree only loosely with the broad thrust of one of the factions, but have their own very different goals for how to carry them out because they disagree with their leaders. There are going to be young Sidereals who only pretend to belong to a faction, who are actually independents who quietly discuss among themselves what Third Option would be best. There might be a few independents who really don't have any opinion about what to do, but most of them are likely to care enough to have their own idea about what should be done. I think very few of the younger Sidereals, possibly none of them, will be so blinded by the Curse that they think the current plan is working perfectly and requires no changes. </div> </div> </div>This is the first thing you've said I agree with without reservation. It basically boils down to &quot;the Sidereals are people and don't march in lockstep.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. It's a Time of Tumult in Creation. The Empress disappearing and the Solars returning kicked the legs out from under a lot of people and now there's a chance for real change, for good or for ill. Even the oldest Bronze Faction member recognizes that things have to change without the Empress around, and they're written as recognizing that. &quot;What are we going to do about the Realm now&quot; is a huge Sidereal plot point discussed in the text.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:49:20-07:00","id":684499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684495#post684495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really...in the First Age, the Sidereals largely operated as advisers and planners. If the Solars had an idea that they wanted to Fate-check, they called up a few Sidereals and had them cast prophecies to see how it would go. If a Lunar was hunting a Wyld Incursion, they could just Infallible Messenger a Siddie and say 'Hey, could you look for Fate disruptions in this general area? I'm trying to locate where they are coming out of the Wyld.' Yeah, they'd still go do field work...some stuff needs the touch of a Chosen of Fate...but they were much less overworked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shit. I just realized Sidereals are Project Managers that laid off all the Developers (Soalrs) because they fucked with the PM's Gnatt Chart. So now the PMs are stuck trying to develop the Application with only the Technical Support (Dragonblooded) and the Testers (Lunars) keep ripping the application apart.<br /> <br /> Okay. My analogy fell apart there at the end, but it amused me so I posted it anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-01-2015, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:00:25-07:00","id":684506,"title":"","content":"Coik says a lot of good things, but I want to add: it undercuts the thesis, not only of the Sidereals as a splat, but of Exalted's theme of larger-than-life heroes capable of untold horrors as laid down in the 1e Core, if we take the reading that the Great Prophecy is a dumbass chump idea that every Sidereal should have known better than to take seriously for even a minute.<br /> <br /> Now, it can still be <i>presented</i> badly (and has). But to paraphrase dev comments: &quot;The solution to 'being able to turn into animals is lame' isn't to get rid of animal shapeshifting, it's to make animals awesome instead of crappy.&quot; The solution to the Great Prophecy coming off as kind of dumb isn't to assume that none of it should matter in Year Zero of Exalted, it's for the 3E Sidereal hardback to do it better, because &quot;if the Solars are gone, Creation will surely survive in a diminished form&quot; versus &quot;if we try to reform the Solars, Creation might be blessed beyond measure but also might be destroyed&quot; versus &quot;if we do nothing, Creation is 100% surely fucked&quot; is a very compelling and powerful idea to have lurking in the background of the setting!<br /> <br /> Also, with specific regard to the Great Contagion, I'd say that &quot;surviving, albeit notably lessened&quot; exactly describes the result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:01:10-07:00","id":684507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684478#post684478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this thread started with Sidereal politics, <a href=\"http://www.doctorshrugs.com/foxhound/comic.php?id=300\" target=\"_blank\">here's</a> Psycho Mantis and Revolver Ocelot discussing them. I'd post the most relevant section but Imageshack seems to be having issues at the moment...</div> </div> </div> </div>Coik, have I told you lately that you are my favorite one?<br /> <br /> Also too: apropos of nothing, the phrase &quot;unique super-powered freak model of warfare&quot; is one I've been using regularly ever since I read that comic.<br /> <br /> God, I miss Last Days of Foxhound.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:04:33-07:00","id":684514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684478#post684478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This assertion fundamentally misunderstands the Great Prophecy. The Great Prophecy was not Kejak and friends shaking a Magic Eight Ball and getting three fortune cookies spat out. The Great Prophecy was a thousand thousand prophecies, cast by the entire Fivescore Fellowship, to the furthest reaches of the Loom (remember this was written when most Sidereal prophecy Charms required at least three Sidereals of different castes to work, and were more effective the more Sidereals present. Even that presupposes that the best way to mechanically represent the Great Prophecy is through Charms, or that it should be mechanically representatable at all)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is interesting (and not indicated at all by the books I own.) So it's more that out of all the prophecies that they saw, every one of them started with the Sidereals doing one of the same three things? That still doesn't necessarily exclude the possibility of them having made other choices... for example, they could have asked the Maidens for advice (assuming that the Great Prophecy didn't already involve that -- I don't think it should be represented mechanically) or gotten the Lunars to overthrow the Solars instead, or all become akuma (not saying that would be a <i><b>good</b></i> idea, but it was probably an option!). Or did those latter 2 ideas show up as well, but were considered variations of Vision of Bronze and Vision of Darkness, respectively?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684478#post684478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it presumes such monumental arrogance and stupidity on the part of the Sidereals that it goes beyond &quot;tragic flaw&quot; into &quot;grotesque parody.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, that's why it bothers me!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684478#post684478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I can see where you're coming from...I'm usually the first person in line bitching about how Sidereals are portrayed as monumental idiots who put their hats on their feet and shoes on their hands. But it's important to remember that it's a problem with <i>portrayal</i> and not supposed to be taken as how Sidereals actually are in setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I don't disagree that their depiction is a problem. But then, how <i><b>should</b></i> they be portrayed? If they were not totally blinded by the Curse, what would their plans look like instead, in your mind? (I honestly want to know... I want a headcannon that makes them less dumb.) This is like asking: &quot;If the Lunars weren't portrayed as sitting on their hands for 1500 years, what would they have been accomplishing?&quot; And the answer is... probably so different we'd have to entirely rewrite the history of the Second Age, or at least the history of the Age of Sorrows, because the Bronze Faction would have reacted to the Great Contagion by changing their methods <i><b>far</b></i> more than in canon, or even having a whole new Prophecy, because they'd realize something had gone way far afield of all their predictions and plans, and that their original prophecy had not accounted for something outside of Fate. (Hence, for the Lunars analogy: the 3E team are rewriting 2nd Age history to give the Lunars some more accomplishments and a more significant part in the setting.)<br /> <br /> It's particularly galling to me that they didn't even plan for the threats that had already harmed the Old Realm: faerie invasion (which had happened before) and a free Primordial attacking (there are still 1 or 2 hostile Primordials out there). The Shogunate wasn't equipped with any way to counter known fae and Primordial threats -- even the Sword of Creation sat unopened for centuries. Likewise, having faced the Great Contagion and now knowing that's also a threat, they have devised... zero ways to prevent another one. That's not smart planning.<br /> <br /> With the setting as written... that's why I'm saying that if the Curse can turn Sidereals into total loonies (and if it does that to Lunars and Solars, it surely does to Sidereals too) then only the elders are actually going to be that truly head-up-ass crazy, and the younger ones are probably almost all much more sensible and not 100% on-board with <i><b>every</b></i>thing their elders tell them to do. And of course, not always agreeing with each other either. Hence my idea of there being lots of sub-agendas and disagreements and quiet dissent within the supposedly unified ranks of each faction. They'll also likely do that simply because, when there are only really two groups you can belong to, each one is obligated to either accept a wide spectrum of viewpoints under their &quot;umbrella&quot; or get really harsh about kicking out dissidents. And neither faction does the latter AFAIK, so they have to put up with the former.<br /> <br /> (I do accept Mercushio's correction that independents aren't always politically impotent.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684478#post684478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...do I even need to address this one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I'd like to know why you think ... I'm not sure what you think here. I can't read between lines to what you're implying. That actually their plans are were working perfectly fine in RY 762 and they hadn't made any mistakes up till then? That it's another example of bad portrayal (and in that case what would you want to portray instead)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-01-2015, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:11:13-07:00","id":684520,"title":"","content":"This drifts a bit off topic, and is meant only as an observation, but that the Realm has been stable for 750 years is actually not quite so impressive if you instead look at that not as mortal generations (19 by quick, bad math) but Dragonblooded Generations (maybe 8?)<br /> <br /> I mean, an empire staying stable through 8 generations is still damn impressive. I'm not sure that there is any real world empire that didn't have at least one major shakeup in 8 generations, but it's not as impressive as 19 mortal ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:29:40-07:00","id":684555,"title":"","content":"DBs don't necessarily wait until they're 100 to start having kids, DaWaterRat. The number of DB generations is probably closer to the number of mortal generations than your estimate would indicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:41:29-07:00","id":684564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684498#post684498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we talking about Creation or are we talking about the Realm and its satrapies? Those sets do not completely overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am talking about <i><b>all</b></i> of Creation, looked at as a <i><b>whole</b></i>. Because the Sidereals should have planned to keep <i><b>all</b></i> of Creation intact, not keep the Blessed Isle intact and shrug as the rest of the world dies. If a few wealthy people are prosperous in the Realm, that does not automatically mean that having the Realm as the sole superpower is good for everybody in every part of Creation. The DBs defend the Realm, but only the Realm and nothing else. (By Threshold, I mean <i><b>everything</b></i> that isn't the Blessed Isle. Not just the coast of the Inner Sea.)<br /> <br /> I think you and I have to agree to disagree about the rightness and goodness and safety of the global situation in RY 762, or the badness of the Great Contagion.<br /> <br /> I don't believe that every single Sidereal is going to believe that the current situation is just fine. Some are going to have a different perspectives because, again, they aren't a hive mind. And just because a Sidereal doesn't think the current plan is working well, doesn't mean they think Solars or Lunars are the solution. I think some of them are going to realize that the Realm is not the <i><b>only</b></i> possible Dragon-Blooded regime that could ever possibly exist, and talk about alternatives <i><b>within</b></i> the Bronze Faction. That is why I say that <i><b>both</b></i> factions will have multiple conflicting viewpoints and sub-agendas within them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:48:14-07:00","id":684570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684520#post684520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This drifts a bit off topic, and is meant only as an observation, but that the Realm has been stable for 750 years is actually not quite so impressive if you instead look at that not as mortal generations (19 by quick, bad math) but Dragonblooded Generations (maybe 8?)<br /> <br /> I mean, an empire staying stable through 8 generations is still damn impressive. I'm not sure that there is any real world empire that didn't have at least one major shakeup in 8 generations, but it's not as impressive as 19 mortal ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>One generation is only 20 years, so it'd be more like 38 of them since the founding of the Realm. Dragon-Blooded also go from birth to graduation in only about 22 years, so it'd be pretty close to the mortal numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:49:32-07:00","id":684571,"title":"","content":"I guess it depends on what you consider a major shake-up.<br /> <br /> The British Empire, from its establishment (as Britain... one could argue that England was already an Empire, as it had American colonies, but I wouldn't really call it that in any serious sense) to decolonisation, went through 14 generations of monarchs (and monarchs tend to have longer generations than working-class people).<br /> <br /> If you were to put it from, say, the loss of the US to the loss of most of Ireland, ie its period of sustained advancement, it's still 7 generations.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's the most successful empire ever (and one with a very stable political system, which only gradually, and peacefully changed from 1688 until now). The biggest land Empire, the Mongols, ran into trouble much, much quicker than that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm... you know, considering how there's 13 Houses that no longer exist, it's entirely possible that the Realm has had several major shake-ups, the books just haven't really gone into them. The houses that tried to seize power, for example, which could have caused large-scale civil war.<br /> Perh\u200baps religious strife too: maybe the Immaculate Order once worked very differently, but was changed in some kind of reformation. Or perhaps there was a schism, leading to several decades of unrest, until one side successfully crushed the other.<br /> Still, I suppose\u200b nothing too dramatic could have happened, as the Empress stayed in charge the entire time.<br /> <br /> Actually, in that sense, it's one generation: succession (either a war over succession, or inheritance by a weak or incompetent ruler) is normally the cause of an empire fracturing, its founder normally holds it together successfully through the life. For example, the Mongols.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-01-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:51:11-07:00","id":684574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684564#post684564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am talking about <i><b>all</b></i> of Creation, looked at as a <i><b>whole</b></i>. Because the Sidereals should have planned to keep <i><b>all</b></i> of Creation intact, not keep the Blessed Isle intact and shrug as the rest of the world dies. If a few wealthy people are prosperous in the Realm, that does not automatically mean that having the Realm as the sole superpower is good for everybody in every part of Creation. The DBs defend the Realm, but only the Realm and nothing else. (By Threshold, I mean <i><b>everything</b></i> that isn't the Blessed Isle. Not just the coast of the Inner Sea.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not what the term &quot;Threshold&quot; means.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals <i>did</i> plan to keep as much of Creation as possible intact. That worked pretty great until the Crusade and the Contagion rolled through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:51:15-07:00","id":684576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684555#post684555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs don't necessarily wait until they're 100 to start having kids, DaWaterRat. The number of DB generations is probably closer to the number of mortal generations than your estimate would indicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>My number of mortal generations is based on a generation of 40 years, not 20, which is why I used 100 for DB generations","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:52:51-07:00","id":684577,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but why would you do that? If your definition of &quot;generation&quot; is gonna be different, you probably ought to note that up front so folks don't get confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-01-2015, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:55:00-07:00","id":684580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684577#post684577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but why would you do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's the Biblical Generaion, for one, which I think is supposed to represent birth to &quot;head of household&quot; status, or the point at which a person has political influence in the community. And by that, there's been maybe 3-4 Dragonblooded generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T11:27:38-07:00","id":684674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684574#post684574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not what the term &quot;Threshold&quot; means.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So then what is the word for everything outside the Blessed Isle?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684574#post684574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereals <i>did</i> plan to keep as much of Creation as possible intact. That worked pretty great until the Crusade and the Contagion rolled through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it did! It looked like it was working pretty well. That was the actual Vision of Bronze.<br /> <br /> It is not working anymore. The Great Curse may blind some Sidereals to that... but it can't blind them all, because the Contagion and shadowlands and Wyld zones are large things. And not everyone who notices problems or threats to Creation will agree with the Gold Faction. I would also hope that at least some Sidereals have enough compassion for mortals to dislike the way most are suffering. Some young Sidereals will say &quot;This Realm, it isn't really the best way to organize Dragon-Blooded, and Creation faces several known threats that the Realm isn't strong enough to stop. We should try to do better with the Dragon-Blooded. Not Solars or Lunars, obviously.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't intend to start a tangent although I knew it was a risk (and I still really want to know how Coik would portray the elders as non-idiots). My main point actually was that within each faction there would be multiple viewpoints on how to achieve their Vision, and not everyone would like how their leader was persuing that Vision or what they were sacrificing to get there... and I actually wanted to talk about those other viewpoints and the internal mini-coalitions, and even cooperation between factions and with independents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-01-2015, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T12:35:11-07:00","id":684741,"title":"","content":"I think an unambiguous statement of the Vision of Bronze being no longer viable is not helpful to the credibility of certain characters, or versatility of games.<br /> <br /> Much the same as any statement from developers that Creation may be past saving or that the return of the Solars might actually finish it shouldn't have a definitive statement of what such an end of the world might look like.<br /> <br /> Their practical application for gameplay is largely in setting a mood and informing the motivations of certain characters anyway.<br /> <br /> I think John put it fairly well one time when he articulated the resurgence of interest in the Gold Faction from coming out of Sidereals no longer seeing the diminishing of the world as being worth it. I certainly think it helps the credibility of Sidereals when even the ones on opposite sides see the other position as <i>functional</i>, if not desirable.<br /> <br /> Although I don't care much for most people's ideas of how to pursue the Gold Vision either.<br /> <br /> It's all looks too much like trying to decode the books for secret insights into the nature of the game world in order to find the one correct solution, rather than a set of contexts in which actors do things.<br /> <br /> Although I'll also note that another detail of my current image of Fate is that prophecy is less a picture of the future and more a kind of directly invoked omen.<br /> <br /> Among other things, that helps keep it from having anything to do with the original question.<br /> <br /> So the Vision of Bronze still works, because keeping the Solars from controlling the world is still a perfectly valid position on how to deal with Solars.<br /> <br /> Something at the core of all this, to make the whole thing hold together from the outset, is to <i><b>never</b></i> compare the Visions in terms of uncertainty versus guarantee.<br /> <br /> After all, approaching the Vision of Bronze from the position of &quot;once we started, we were certain to stop the Solars and save the world&quot; doesn't do much for the credibility of Solars either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T12:36:33-07:00","id":684752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684674#post684674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So then what is the word for everything outside the Blessed Isle?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't really one. &quot;The Threshold&quot; is the thin ring of land around the Inland Sea. The term is sometimes used to mean &quot;the satrapies&quot; but its actually somewhat amorphous; An-Teng, for example, would be considered part of the Threshold despite the fact that it extends a great distance inland. Greyfalls would not, despite being a satrapy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it did! It looked like it was working pretty well. That was the actual Vision of Bronze.<br /> <br /> It is not working anymore. </div> </div> </div>Mmm, yes and no. The Vision of Bronze was that without the Solars, Creation would continue, but in a lessened form. That's still happening. Creation wasn't awesome in the Age of Sorrows, hence the name, but at least until the Empress disappeared it was stable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also hope that at least some Sidereals have enough compassion for mortals to dislike the way most are suffering. Some young Sidereals will say &quot;This Realm, it isn't really the best way to organize Dragon-Blooded, and Creation faces several known threats that the Realm isn't strong enough to stop. We should try to do better with the Dragon-Blooded. Not Solars or Lunars, obviously.&quot; </div> </div> </div>They will say that, yes. And their Elders will say &quot;Okay, kid. Come up with a viable plan that has acceptable risk.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, though. Once upon a time, the Dragon-Blooded were organized much differently. That was called the Shogunate. It had a lot more fancy First Age gear and it ruled the entire world in the wreckage of the Old Realm... but it also wasn't all that stable. The Dragon-Blooded were constantly at war with each other in pursuit of power and glory, draining off Creation's resources in the process. The Shogunate was decent at keeping the Fair Folk out (and back then the Deathlords were just a whisper and a rumor) but that was basically it.<br /> <br /> The Realm is actually better then the Shogunate from this perspective, because the Realm has the Defense Grid, which is better than the whole Shogunate put together at keeping out the Fair Folk and probably would be the Deathlords as well; Juggernaut would be a smoking crater if the Empress were still around.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded are also incapable of maintaining First Age infrastructure at anything larger than the level Lookshy is at. Even with Sidereal help.<br /> <br /> So if you don't want to back the Gold Faction, what you need to do is come up with a way to transition to something 1) different from the Realm, 2) different from the Shogunate, because that's been tried and wasn't much better, that 3) works better than both of them, and 4) works enough better that you can either convince the Scarlet Empress to go along with it or convince enough other Sidereals it is time for Usurpation II: This Time Its Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> Now, with the Empress gone, you don't really need to worry about 4 anymore, but that's still a supremely tall order.<br /> <br /> You are absolutely right that the Bronze Faction has had its legs kicked out from under with with Scarlet gone; it is known that a Dragon-Blooded can control the Defense Grid, but Scarlet was a singular individual and it isn't known that she's replaceable in that sense. This sort of sucks the air out of the Bronze Faction, which is sort of spinning its wheels trying to figure out how to salvage their whole Realm project... and most of that air is going right to the Gold Faction, whose pitch is basically &quot;We get to re-train the Solars literally from scratch, knowing now what we didn't know then. They can probably make peace between us and the Lunars and are equipped to stabilize Creation and rebuild it.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want a third option, you gotta compete with those two, and that's hard, especially because your third option has to also somehow deal with the Solars as well. The Sidereals just went from having to deal with 300 Lunars and a few random Solars to a ton of both, plus extra Abyssal and Infernal goodness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main point actually was that within each faction there would be multiple viewpoints on how to achieve their Vision, and not everyone would like how their leader was persuing that Vision or what they were sacrificing to get there... and I actually wanted to talk about those other viewpoints and the internal mini-coalitions, and even cooperation between factions and with independents. </div> </div> </div>This seems fairly uncontroversial, yes. Lupo has been mentioned in this thread. Loyal Gold Faction Sidereal. Doesn't agree 100% with how Ayesha does things. Follows her lead, and is loyal, but also does his own thing to the extent he's able.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T12:59:28-07:00","id":684781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684741#post684741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an unambiguous statement of the Vision of Bronze being no longer viable is not helpful to the credibility of certain characters, or versatility of games.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684752#post684752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm, yes and no. The Vision of Bronze was that without the Solars, Creation would continue, but in a lessened form. That's still happening. Creation wasn't awesome in the Age of Sorrows, hence the name, but at least until the Empress disappeared it was stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is my <i><b>contention</b></i> that the Vision of Bronze clearly ended because Creation is Doomed, the Deathlords as-written have been on-track to destroy Creation at least since the Great Contagion, and it's only a matter of time. Furthermore, the Contagion-level threats can easily wipe out the whole world and nobody is equipped to do anything about it, which also calls into quesition the notion that the Wyld Hunt is <i><b>all</b></i> you need to keep Creation safe for eternity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684741#post684741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Vision of Bronze still works, because keeping the Solars from controlling the world is still a perfectly valid position on how to deal with Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a sneaky way of saying they horribly misinterpreted it from the start?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684741#post684741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, approaching the Vision of Bronze from the position of &quot;once we started, we were certain to stop the Solars and save the world&quot; doesn't do much for the credibility of Solars either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The assumption of total certainly is the arrogance. Which, by itself, would be a tragic flaw instead of a grotesque parody, to misquote Coik.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684741#post684741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's all looks too much like trying to decode the books for secret insights into the nature of the game world in order to find the one correct solution, rather than a set of contexts in which actors do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more suggesting that characters, from their limited perspectives, would be offering other ideas. Not that we as players should try to find the OOCly best possible idea. If the game can be &quot;solved&quot; like a sudoku it isn't as interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684752#post684752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They will say that, yes. And their Elders will say &quot;Okay, kid. Come up with a viable plan that has acceptable risk.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course the elders won't listen, they're convinced they're right and everyone else is wrong, end of discussion. That's why the younger Sids are going to do things against orders or secretly or try to persuade colleagues of their views, or pursue their goals by trading favors with whoever or opposing a co-faction member unexpectedly.<br /> <br /> I agree the Shogunate was worse than the Realm in not having a Realm Defense Grid. I don't know much about how they treated mortals and if they systematically pillaged the (outer directions? non-core provinces? whatevers) into poverty. They did have more infrastructure than the Realm has preserved. They failed to stop the Great Contagion... but the Realm and Sidereals have no defenses against that either. The Shogunate protected all of Creation, while the Realm can't protect everything and doesn't even try to protect all that they could protect, because the Dyasts' goals are primarily to get richer by pillaging. The idea of resting everything in the Realm upon one Empress looks like an attempt to avoid the succession problems the Shogunate had, but it swings so far in the opposite direction that it depends on making her literally immortal and then never letting anything bad happen to her forever and, well, that was a silly plan. And what if instead of disappearing she had quietly gone akuma, or senile, and stayed on the throne?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684752#post684752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you don't want to back the Gold Faction, what you need to do is come up with a way to transition to something 1) different from the Realm, 2) different from the Shogunate, because that's been tried and wasn't much better, that 3) works better than both of them, and 4) works enough better that you can either convince the Scarlet Empress to go along with it or convince enough other Sidereals it is time for Usurpation II: This Time Its Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> Now, with the Empress gone, you don't really need to worry about 4 anymore, but that's still a supremely tall order.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some Sidereals would have thought about this well before the Empress vanished. I think some of the Bronze Faction at the time Scarlet was settling down on the throne would have disagreed with Kejak about how the Empire was being organized, and how the Immaculate Philosophy was being altered. I think some would have asked what the plan was to protect Creation from another Contagion, and not be satisfied with &quot;Hope it never happens again, I guess.&quot; I don't think those disagreements would all go away. And after Scarlet vanishes, surely some Bronze Stars are going to say &quot;Maybe instead of an Empire we should try to steer the Dragon-Blooded into a less eggs-in-one-basket direction.&quot; The Dynasts are worried about the survival of their society as well, many of them don't want a civil war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684752#post684752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems fairly uncontroversial, yes. Lupo has been mentioned in this thread. Loyal Gold Faction Sidereal. Doesn't agree 100% with how Ayesha does things. Follows her lead, and is loyal, but also does his own thing to the extent he's able.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any canon examples of Bronze Sidereals who don't agree with everything Kejak tells them? Or good examples among Bronze player characters?<br /> <br /> For that matter, are there any canon examples of independents, or good examples of independent PCs, who agree with each other about anything substantial? How much are their political views depicted, other than &quot;don't want to do what either faction is doing.&quot; To go back to the (admittedly not entirely apt) U.S. analogy, are they the equivalents of people who vote for/try to organize third parties or other political opposition movements, or the equivalents of people who are completely a-political? They're Exalted so I think the latter sort of apathy is rather unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-01-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:10:22-07:00","id":685797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684514#post684514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's particularly galling to me that they didn't even plan for the threats that had already harmed the Old Realm: faerie invasion (which had happened before) and a free Primordial attacking (there are still 1 or 2 hostile Primordials out there). The Shogunate wasn't equipped with any way to counter known fae and Primordial threats -- even the Sword of Creation sat unopened for centuries. Likewise, having faced the Great Contagion and now knowing that's also a threat, they have devised... zero ways to prevent another one. That's not smart planning.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the only part I'm going to weigh in on because it's a huge one - the Shogunate was <i>absolutely</i> equipped to deal with known threats; a million Dragon-blooded with a Sidereal support tore the mighty from their thrones and banished them <i>forever</i> (Breaking of the Jade Prison notwithstanding). Demonic &amp; Fair Folk incursions were not a major threat during either the High or Low First Age (Single exception; Aftershock War but if I was the Sidereals, I'd also not count on the other escapee from the Titanomachy coming back). The Sword of Creation sat unopened for centuries because it was not necessary. Hands down, Creation's best defence against threats from outside since casting out the Primordials has been the Exalted, and you seem to be under the assumption that the Terrestrial Host is either incompetent or irrelevant.<br /> <br /> And since discovering that the Underworld (and by extension, Deathlords) present an actual threat to the stability of Creation, the Sidereals have an elder permanently assigned down there, and the Conventions on the Underworld &amp; Deathlords aren't exactly sitting idle twiddling their thumbs waiting for the next undead horrorshow to pop up. Hell, Black Ice Shadow being born as a ghostblood was part of their work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:09:25-07:00","id":685834,"title":"","content":"Not irrelevant or completely incompetent. However, it is established fact that the surviving Exalted left over after the Usurpation, not including the Lunars, were less powerful, numerous, and equipped than the united Exalted host that beat back the Dissolution Invasion and Ramethus. It would be incredibly naive to assume they have the exact same ability to beat back every threat and there's no reason to worry. Let alone that it's a good idea to deliberately suppress DB population growth.<br /> <br /> It's part of ignoring everything outside of fate when they made the Great Prophecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-02-2015, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:22:15-07:00","id":685905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684514#post684514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still doesn't necessarily exclude the possibility of them having made other choices... for example, they could have asked the Maidens for advice (assuming that the Great Prophecy didn't already involve that -- I don't think it should be represented mechanically) or gotten the Lunars to overthrow the Solars instead, or all become akuma (not saying that would be a <i><b>good</b></i> idea, but it was probably an option!). Or did those latter 2 ideas show up as well, but were considered variations of Vision of Bronze and Vision of Darkness, respectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Sidereal books...I want to say second edition, but I'd have to pull to be sure...mentioned some Sidereals trying to contact the Maidens for advice, but they weren't taking any calls regarding the Prophecy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, I don't disagree that their depiction is a problem. But then, how <i><b>should</b></i> they be portrayed? If they were not totally blinded by the Curse, what would their plans look like instead, in your mind? (I honestly want to know... I want a headcannon that makes them less dumb.) </div> </div> </div>If you're just asking for my opinion? I think the best way to improve the Sidereals' portrayal without doing substantial rewrites is to show them being active in the management of Creation. Don't just mention the Convention of Deathlords and give a brief description of it, include a line like &quot;The Convention is currently testing methods to sped cleansing of shadowlands without the need for Solar Circle Sorcery.&quot; That's plot hook and setting development in one, and having 2-3 of them for each Convention and both factions gives an idea of what the Sidereal agenda as a whole looks like while being fairly space efficient.<br /> <br /> On the surface that looks deceptively simple, but I think it would go a long way towards tying the Sidereals more closely to Creation and making them feel proactive, which I've felt is a big problem with Sidereals (and Lunars). It also gets away from the &quot;exception based&quot; setting development, where we're only shown when things go wrong because that's &quot;more interesting&quot; or some rot. I know that's the approach the game took towards Realm satrapies for the longest time, and look how <i>that</i> turned out...even I'm tired of complaining about how weak and ineffective the Realm looks a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> Of course, like I mentioned, that's presupposing that we want to preserve as much of the existing setting as possible while being as space efficient as possible. Holden and hatewheel may well decide that the Bureau of Destiny needs a total rewrite to fit into 3e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I do accept Mercushio's correction that independents aren't always politically impotent.) </div> </div> </div>I'd actually say that Independents are actually <i>rarely</i> politically impotent, particularly in the Age of Sorrows. They may not have a lot of banked political power like the Bronze or be an up-and-comer like the Gold, but with how small a group the Sidereals are, every one of them is important to the overall effort. Look at the American presidiantal election and how important swing states are; that's the Independent Sidereals. As an Independent, there's almost certaintly where you're going to be the deciding vote and get to play kingmaker.<br /> <br /> Just to give my own example, the last game I played in was I was an Independent in the South, which in our game was pretty evenly split between Bronze and Gold. My character made her career (and got several important initiatives off the ground) by playing off Kejak and Ura because they both <i>needed her</i> in order to pursue their agendas in the Convention of Fire. My GM even dropped several hints, some less than subtle, that Kejak was impressed enough with the way she was politically squeezing him that he was grooming her for a leadership position in the Forbidding Manse after he died.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes I'd like to know why you think ... I'm not sure what you think here. I can't read between lines to what you're implying. That actually their plans are were working perfectly fine in RY 762 and they hadn't made any mistakes up till then? That it's another example of bad portrayal (and in that case what would you want to portray instead)? </div> </div> </div>What I was getting at was that both Kejak and Ura are smart enough to know that things never actually go to plan and that adaptability is a valuable trait. I'll certaintly agree that this doesn't come across in the books, particularly in 2e, which took some of the worst parts of fanon about the Sidereal Curse and ran with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:38:01-07:00","id":685917,"title":"","content":"I like the way you think Coik.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=685905#post685905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're just asking for my opinion? I think the best way to improve the Sidereals' portrayal without doing substantial rewrites is to show them being active in the management of Creation. Don't just mention the Convention of Deathlords and give a brief description of it, include a line like &quot;The Convention is currently testing methods to sped cleansing of shadowlands without the need for Solar Circle Sorcery.&quot; That's plot hook and setting development in one, and having 2-3 of them for each Convention and both factions gives an idea of what the Sidereal agenda as a whole looks like while being fairly space efficient.<br /> <br /> On the surface that looks deceptively simple, but I think it would go a long way towards tying the Sidereals more closely to Creation and making them feel proactive, which I've felt is a big problem with Sidereals (and Lunars). It also gets away from the &quot;exception based&quot; setting development, where we're only shown when things go wrong because that's &quot;more interesting&quot; or some rot. I know that's the approach the game took towards Realm satrapies for the longest time, and look how <i>that</i> turned out...even I'm tired of complaining about how weak and ineffective the Realm looks a lot of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Even within the 2E setting that would certainly help give a better impression of the leader doing their real job and proactively protecting Creation. It would also provide a bunch more concrete plot hooks/options for PCs to do things other than take marching orders on faction agendas. Things can include hashing out their own ideas on how to accomplish (Goal XYZ) and whether to work with independents or the other faction to do (non-faction thing for Creation).<br /> <br /> Although it would help even more to also include constructive, <i><b>non-faction</b></i> things they've already accomplished (<i><b>successfully</b></i>) for Creation in the past, otherwise it might give the impression that they only started actively doing that stuff (outside of their faction agendas) in the past 5 years, or that all they did until 5 years ago was fail and make things worse. Hopefully 3E's history overhaul will include that. Including major threats that they actually stopped, successfully and without creating an even bigger threat as a random side-effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-02-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T12:07:17-07:00","id":686035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684741#post684741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I'll also note that another detail of my current image of Fate is that prophecy is less a picture of the future and more a kind of directly invoked omen.<br /> <br /> Among other things, that helps keep it from having anything to do with the original question.<br /> <br /> So the Vision of Bronze still works, because keeping the Solars from controlling the world is still a perfectly valid position on how to deal with Solars.<br /> <br /> Something at the core of all this, to make the whole thing hold together from the outset, is to <i><b>never</b></i> compare the Visions in terms of uncertainty versus guarantee.<br /> <br /> After all, approaching the Vision of Bronze from the position of &quot;once we started, we were certain to stop the Solars and save the world&quot; doesn't do much for the credibility of Solars either.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the bigger issues with the Vision of Bronze is that it was founded on the idea that the Solar Exaltations were locked away, not running around taking an active role in Creation. So long as the Solars are free to go out and about, Creation isn't going to be adhering to the Vision of Bronze. And so far there hasn't been much presented from the Bronze Faction as to how to deal with that.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Bronze Faction's actions seem to be more akin to burying their heads in the sand - &quot;I know that there's 30 times as many Solar Exaltations out these days than there were a few years ago, but don't mind that. Just keep steadily doing what we've been doing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, it's fine if the Vision of Bronze is not viable <i>at the moment</i> because of the Solars, but there should be some sense that the Bronze Faction is coming up with ideas on how to reroute Creation back on the proper course laid out by the Bronze Vision.<br /> <br /> It reminds me a bit of Issac Asimov's Foundation series, where the Mule shows up, blows Hari Seldon's plan to hell and then the Second Foundation works behind the scenes to bring everything &quot;back on course&quot; to conform with his psychohistory predictions. While the Second Foundation got caught with their pants down, and the course of history was suddenly drastically different from what they were expecting, there was a definite sense that they were very competent and were capable of &quot;fixing things,&quot; eventually, and you knew that their plan consisted of more than, &quot;Let's just keep doing what we were doing before the Mule showed up and hope it works.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that a slightly more competent and proactive presentation of the Bronze Faction will help to make their Bronze Vision seem more viable post Year Zero. Including an in-character suggestion or two about ways that Creation can conform to the Bronze Vision even with the Solar Exalted returned to the world or even rewriting the Bronze Vision slightly so that it is still absolutely viable, even with 300 Solar Exalted running around Creation could also do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-02-2015, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T12:29:21-07:00","id":686051,"title":"","content":"From what little I have seen released of Sidereal, I think Third Edition's plan to fix the Visions of Bronze and Gold is to push them to the dust bins of history. Similar to how little the Federalists and Anti-Federalists have an impact on today's US political parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-02-2015, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T12:54:13-07:00","id":686061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684514#post684514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's particularly galling to me that they didn't even plan for the threats that had already harmed the Old Realm: faerie invasion (which had happened before) and a free Primordial attacking (there are still 1 or 2 hostile Primordials out there). The Shogunate wasn't equipped with any way to counter known fae and Primordial threats -- even the Sword of Creation sat unopened for centuries. </div> </div> </div> </div>You're trying to argue a Watsonian point with Doylist evidence. It's not effective.<br /> <br /> None of the &quot;First Age bad shit&quot; events described in 2e (like faerie invasion or loose Primordials) were conceived of at the time that the Prophecies were introduced into the setting in 1e, or expounded on again in the 2e Sids book.<br /> <br /> You seem to be saying the Sidereal plans are bad because whatever author wrote about the Visions (either in 1e or 2e Sids) didn't conceive that some author later in the line would introduce giant setting-shaking events, or that the later author didn't incorporate the effects of those events into future Sidereal planning. Or you're saying that, in-setting, the Sidereals were portrayed as dumb because their actions don't account for stuff that happened later (OOC) but described things that happened before (IC)<br /> <br /> Either way, that's terrible logic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684514#post684514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, having faced the Great Contagion and now knowing that's also a threat, they have devised... zero ways to prevent another one. That's not smart planning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says they're not trying to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:10:23-07:00","id":686099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the bigger issues with the Vision of Bronze is that it was founded on the idea that the Solar Exaltations were locked away, not running around taking an active role in Creation. So long as the Solars are free to go out and about, Creation isn't going to be adhering to the Vision of Bronze.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:25:09-07:00","id":686112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686099#post686099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Vision (at least as presented in the 1st and 2nd edition Sidereal books) showed that the vision requires the Solar Exalted to continually be hunted down and killed or trapped away. At the moment, sending Wyld Hunts after all of the Solar Exalted just isn't possible; there isn't enough manpower, and every year the Solars grow stronger and stronger. Dealing with 300 Solar Exaltations would have been difficult even during the Shogunate when there were 10 to 100 times as many Dragon Blooded - that's why the Sidereal created the Jade Prison to lock the Exaltations away in the first place. <br /> <br /> This is part of the reason why the Bronze Vision appears, on its face, to have failed. The conditions for fulfilling it can't really be met anymore, and so far the gameline hasn't suggested that the Bronze Faction has any new ideas to handle that. So the Bronze Vision needs a bit of a tweak or the Bronze Faction needs to be presented as having some vague ideas of how to deal with this new situation. <br /> <br /> Otherwise the Bronze Faction is going to keep coming across a group that is just stubbornly rallying around an out-of-date and ineffective idea rather than one that is trying to effectively find ways to adapt to a changing world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:40:41-07:00","id":686131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686061#post686061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure entirely what you're saying (I don't know &quot;Watsonian&quot; and &quot;Doylian&quot;). If you mean that the books sort of contradict or talk past each other to build up a somewhat incoherent picture of the past, that undermines some of the narratives of the Sidereals (and Lunars) I don't disagree. I can't easily think about the setting from an unwritten, hypothetical alternate-history perspective, though, only the setting as written or specific headcanons that I've seen written down, like Coik just did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=685905#post685905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually say that Independents are actually <i>rarely</i> politically impotent, particularly in the Age of Sorrows. They may not have a lot of banked political power like the Bronze or be an up-and-comer like the Gold, but with how small a group the Sidereals are, every one of them is important to the overall effort. Look at the American presidiantal election and how important swing states are; that's the Independent Sidereals. As an Independent, there's almost certaintly where you're going to be the deciding vote and get to play kingmaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. However, it won't be the case in every circumstance or for every goal, only some of them. If Faction A wants Option A and Faction B wants Option B, independents get to play tiebreaker (or even coalition builder) between Options A and B... assuming one of those two options appeal to them. If they actually want Option C, and Factions A and B absolutely won't consider it, then the independent's goals are a lot less relevant. The two factions can mostly control what options are on the table in the first place. (This is also common in U.S. politics.)<br /> <br /> This may then become a reason for some, who would rather be independent, to join a faction just to get in the club and get some support or a mentor, but then only sort-of go along with the official agenda. And if the political tide turns, they might be the first to leave, because in a sense they weren't entirely on-board to begin with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684359#post684359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say tools made by Solars, I'm thinking of things like thinking automatons optimised to helping manage the unintuitive workload of destiny management, engines capable of modelling all kinds of life intersections and alternate futures, and even things like writing kits made to allow Sidereals to write out all of the necessary orders and directives to precisely manage enormous numbers of destinies per day in a manner that transcended the physical limits of how much paperwork a human shaped thing can do in that time. Not things that replaced the powers of Sidereals, but complemented them; the kinds of tools that would be useful to somebody with World-Shaping Artistic Vision in a similar way to how a daiklave is useful to somebody with Hungry Tiger Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went back to find this post because I really liked your ideas and... suddenly I wonder why the Sidereals wouldn't still have these tools in their treasuries in Heaven. Are you picturing artifacts that required Solar maintenance?<br /> <br /> (In my mind they are now the Calculating Engine of Probable and Implausible Futures, and the Scribal Assembly of the Efficient Weaver.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-02-2015, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T15:29:46-07:00","id":686206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=684514#post684514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's particularly galling to me that they didn't even plan for the threats that had already harmed the Old Realm: faerie invasion (which had happened before) and a free Primordial attacking (there are still 1 or 2 hostile Primordials out there). The Shogunate wasn't equipped with any way to counter known fae and Primordial threats -- even the Sword of Creation sat unopened for centuries. Likewise, having faced the Great Contagion and now knowing that's also a threat, they have devised... zero ways to prevent another one. That's not smart planning.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, <i>humanity</i> is not full of &quot;smart planning.&quot; Look at Venice. No, really, look at it.<br /> <br /> Second, these things you describe, they're apocalyptic in scope <i>even with the Solars there</i>. One of the things I love about Ex3 is the return to uncertainty - having a Solar on your side is no longer a guarantee that you're going to win. If another Primordial came crawling out of the woodwork, yeah, <i>maybe</i> this hypothetical United Exalted Host as a whole could ride him down and murder him before he rendered Creation so uninhabitable that it has to be abandoned. Likewise the Solars may have been able to contain the Great Contagion before it took billions of lives, but I feel like a setting where there was no chance of them not doing it would be a pretty boring one.<br /> <br /> You might as well call <i>us</i> shitty planners for not being able to prevent another mass out of space striking the Earth out of nowhere hard enough to gouge out the Moon - sure, it's <i>happened before</i>, but that in no way implies that anything we have is big enough to throw at the problem. Now pretend that we've had to destroy, decommission, or outlaw our most powerful weapons to prevent the psychos in charge of the world from turning them on each other and destroying the Earth as collateral damage (you don't even have to pretend on that one, because we're already in the process of doing so)! Losing the ability to maybe break up a potential Moon-gouging mass by bombarding it with space lasers is an acceptable sacrifice for keeping space lasers out of the hands of people who would definitely turn them on our own planet.<br /> <br /> For that matter, how about the Sun? No, I'm not talking about the god, for a change, but rather, that bright and hateful thing that stabs me in the eyes every time I leave work! We had a geomagnetic storm back in 1859 that was paired up with a nasty solar flare; this caused wires to be overloaded with current, knocking out communications and even setting some equipment on fire.<br /> <br /> So what have we done since then? <i>Covered the Earth in wires</i>, of course! Millions of them! Billions of them! If the 1859 storm hit us today, <b>we would be fucked</b>, with the damage to the U.S. alone being measured as, potentially, <i>trillions of dollars</i>. <br /> <br /> But I guess we're just &quot;poor planners,&quot; right?<br /> <br /> Also, just to clarify, &quot;Doylist&quot; versus &quot;Watsonian&quot; refers to the difference in analyzing elements of a work of fiction from the perspective of someone writing it (Sir Arthur Conan Doyle, author of the Sherlock Holmes stories) versus someone inside it (Doctor Watson, a character in the Sherlock Holmes stories).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-02-2015, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T15:38:49-07:00","id":686211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686131#post686131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure entirely what you're saying (I don't know &quot;Watsonian&quot; and &quot;Doylian&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alucard's already addressed this, but hey. &quot;Watsonian&quot; refers to the use of a fictional work's internal or in-universe logic, where &quot;Doylist&quot; refers to a logic from reasons outside that fictional work. Consider a C-movie's last-minute reveal that the protagonist pulls superpowers out of nowhere. A Watsonian explanation could be that the protagonist was actually an angel all along, who needed to do everything the way it did because of some big unexplored cosmic plan. The Doylist explanation could be that the writer just stopped caring and/or just found out there wasn't going to be the sequel that was originally promised and needed to wrap things up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a good point. However, it won't be the case in every circumstance or for every goal, only some of them. If Faction A wants Option A and Faction B wants Option B, independents get to play tiebreaker (or even coalition builder) between Options A and B... assuming one of those two options appeal to them. If they actually want Option C, and Factions A and B absolutely won't consider it, then the independent's goals are a lot less relevant. The two factions can mostly control what options are on the table in the first place. (This is also common in U.S. politics.) </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, it's not between Option A and B. It's between (Option A plus whatever that side's offering in exchange for the cooperation) and (Option B plus whatever the other side's offering). Depending on the situation and Sidereal, all options could be found odious on the face of them, but the deal one side is giving is sweet enough to the Independent to sway that character.<br /> <br /> You're correct that it's not going to happen every time. It does still give them a certain contextual and circumstantial amount of power that's not to be had as a member of either Faction. Power which might be seen as more of a bonus than anything else, if the Sidereal in question disagrees strongly enough with both Factions' agendas to not want to work toward them, or, say, has some other agenda from which the Sidereal would rather not be distracted to the degree both Factions would demand. It depends on the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T15:52:15-07:00","id":686219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686211#post686211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Watsonian&quot; refers to the use of a fictional work's internal or in-universe logic, where &quot;Doylist&quot; refers to a logic from reasons outside that fictional work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> I guess if something doesn't make enough sense to have a &quot;Watsonian&quot; explanation I tend to throw up my hands and stop caring about the story altogether. Or write off the nonsensical character as insane/stupid. That may seem uncharitable but plenty of real human behavior looks both insane and stupid to me.<br /> (See also: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poe&#39;s_law\" target=\"_blank\">Poe's Law</a>.)<br /> <br /> (Also it didn't occur to me at all to compare publication dates.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686211#post686211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking, it's not between Option A and B. It's between (Option A plus whatever that side's offering in exchange for the cooperation) and (Option B plus whatever the other side's offering).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Something that wouldn't as often be seen as necessary to offer to a fellow member of the same faction, you mean? So that instead of only helping decide between what the 2 factions want to do, sometimes they have enough leverage to get a separate thing of their own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-02-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T16:00:46-07:00","id":686245,"title":"","content":"To be fair Alucard, there isn't a cabal of nigh immortal magical demigods with the power to not only see into the future, but actually decide what will happen, and who were created and tasked with specifically protecting the Earth and humanity from existential threats. While humans do often do dumb things without considering the future, I don't know that the same statement is exactly applicable when dealing with godlings who literally sit down and plan out the future of the world every week.<br /> <br /> But yes, if there was a secret cabal of miracle working puppeteers who controlled most of the Earth and could actually see into and plan out the future, and then bad stuff happened because they didn't bother to plan for it, calling them shitty planners would be entirely fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-02-2015, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T16:04:03-07:00","id":686248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686219#post686219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you.<br /> I guess if something doesn't make enough sense to have a &quot;Watsonian&quot; explanation I tend to throw up my hands and stop caring about the story altogether. Or write off the nonsensical character as insane/stupid. That may seem uncharitable but plenty of real human behavior looks both insane and stupid to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually, I'm the same way but I give Role Playing Games a bit of leeway due to the need to create a balanced game setting that is fun to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T16:38:47-07:00","id":686258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686245#post686245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair Alucard, there isn't a cabal of nigh immortal magical demigods with the power to not only see into the future, but actually decide what will happen</div> </div> </div> </div>Always in motion, the future is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T17:35:58-07:00","id":686300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686258#post686258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always in motion, the future is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember Yoda hosting meetings in his swamp, where a bunch of gods would show up and they would sit down to hammer out what was going to happen in the galaxy and what kind of ramifications those actions would have fifty years or one-hundred years down the line. To paraphrase, when it comes to dealing with the future, hokey visions and strange dreams are no match for a good Bureau of Destiny planning committee, kid. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T18:46:03-07:00","id":686316,"title":"","content":"My point being, free will is a Thing, so predestination isn't, and thus the ability to predict long-run specifics, versus short-run macro-level trends, is also limited","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T19:00:15-07:00","id":686325,"title":"","content":"Sure free will is a thing. At the same time though, planning out the future is also the Sidereal's thing. It's only natural that they would consider and think about what's going to be happening 50 or 100 years from now, in ways that, for example, people in our world never would. In fact, I would imagine that if a Sidereal decided to enact some action on Fate to ensure something would happen, they would be remiss if they <i>didn't</i> explore, map out and consider the long-term fallout that might arise from doing something like that, as well as how that might affect other on-going plans other people have for Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-02-2015, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T19:02:39-07:00","id":686326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686245#post686245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair Alucard, there isn't a cabal of nigh immortal magical demigods with the power to not only see into the future, but actually decide what will happen\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Magical demigods, yes. <br /> <br /> Nigh-immortal, no. We've already determined they have a decent turnover rate. <br /> <br /> Seeing the future? Sorta - absent some very specific, limited-scope Charms, Sidereal future knowledge mostly comes from their membership in various committees, and their connections. Considering that the system they're rooted in is broken and corrupt pretty much from top to bottom, stuff can blindside them. Stuff can blindside anyone. And it doesn't even have to be the work of a Third Circle Demon or some shit; it could just be that the tiger-headed god assigned to watch this area decided to foist his duties on someone incapable of actually doing his job, and fucked off to this Great Forks place everyone keeps talking about.<br /> <br /> <i>Deciding</i> the future? Perhaps in the broadest sense. But they're far from the top of the heap of a corrupt, broken system. Don't get me wrong, their power and influence are great, but balanced against it is a whole heap of responsibility, and honestly I wouldn't rank Sidereal ability to &quot;decide the future&quot; much higher than having folks on the board of directors of Walmart Stores, Inc., in the House of Representatives, in the higher circles of the Mafia, and having ties to the Vatican by way of some cardinals. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686245#post686245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and who were created and tasked with specifically protecting the Earth and humanity from existential threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't take this line seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686245#post686245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While humans do often do dumb things without considering the future, I don't know that the same statement is exactly applicable when dealing with godlings who literally sit down and plan out the future of the world every week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the &quot;godlings&quot; part, <i>how</i> is that different from our world?<br /> <br /> You're acting like Heaven is this big monolith. It's not. It's a huge, vast wad of fractious and competing committees.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686245#post686245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, if there was a secret cabal of miracle working puppeteers who controlled most of the Earth and could actually see into and plan out the future, and then bad stuff happened because they didn't bother to plan for it, calling them shitty planners would be entirely fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>The politics jokes that spring immediately to mind are a tad too grim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-02-2015, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T19:08:19-07:00","id":686327,"title":"","content":"The fact is, in this game (or in the setting), there should be no such thing as a guaranteed outcome, and there certainly shouldn't be one hundreds to thousands of years in advance just because an Exalt used their magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T19:32:57-07:00","id":686337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686326#post686326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're acting like Heaven is this big monolith. It's not. It's a huge, vast wad of fractious and competing committees.<br /> <br /> The politics jokes that spring immediately to mind are a tad too grim.</div> </div> </div> </div>In our world, pretty much nobody makes decisions on what might happen a century ahead because they'll be dead by then. In Heaven, which is composed of Sidereal who can expect to live for 2000-3000 years and gods, who can expect to live for millions of years, it seems rather strange they wouldn't be looking a century or two down the road and thinking about what would happen and what sort of result a given action might trigger decades down the road.<br /> <br /> That's why I feel that comparing the planners of our own world, who are lucky to live for 80 years, with Creation's Fate planners, most of whom are either immortal (or might as well be from the perspective of a normal human) is a bogus comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-02-2015, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T19:59:59-07:00","id":686386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686337#post686337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which is composed of Sidereal who can expect to live for 2000-3000 years</div> </div> </div> </div>This hasn't been true since maybe before the Usurpation, what with all the &quot;getting killed by Lunars&quot; that very frequently goes on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T21:44:45-07:00","id":686457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686386#post686386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This hasn't been true since maybe before the Usurpation, what with all the &quot;getting killed by Lunars&quot; that very frequently goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>While an amusing meme, we don't have hard numbers on the turnover rate of Sidereal Exalted. Whatever their numbers are, a newly Exalted Sidereal can safely expect to live for much longer than a normal human's lifespan. Furthermore their Exaltation is largely based around looking with and dealing with the future and they spend their time planning for the future alongside immortal beings for whom a decade is like an eye blink. That's is why I find it kind of awkward when people claim that a Sidereal's standards for planning the future would be little different from that of an average non-magical human's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T00:23:12-07:00","id":686637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686219#post686219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess if something doesn't make enough sense to have a &quot;Watsonian&quot; explanation I tend to throw up my hands and stop caring about the story altogether. Or write off the nonsensical character as insane/stupid. That may seem uncharitable but plenty of real human behavior looks both insane and stupid to me.<br /> (See also: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poe&#39;s_law\" target=\"_blank\">Poe's Law</a>.) </div> </div> </div>Understandable. Different people have different standards for suspending their disbelief or letting a perceived incongruity go with the presumption that there's just something one is missing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hm. Something that wouldn't as often be seen as necessary to offer to a fellow member of the same faction, you mean? So that instead of only helping decide between what the 2 factions want to do, sometimes they have enough leverage to get a separate thing of their own? </div> </div> </div>Right. It's presumed making such extra offers to a fellow Faction member wouldn't be so often necessary: all Faction members in theory benefit intrinsically from advancing one of their Faction's goals,* so advancing it is often benefit enough. It varies by the situation, but Independents aren't always in the same boat. And if which way the Independent goes is liable to tip the scales one way or the other, both Factions have an incentive to persuade that Independent to go their way. Which can easily take the form of something like...<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, we both know you couldn't care less about this decision. Buuuuut a little bird told me about a certain sorcerous experiment that's hit a dead-end. You've been drawing on the decrypted works of the Moonrise-Piercing Artisan, correct? Well! I noticed that three of her recently recovered volumes are on track to be cleared for Bureau use, but the earliest is at least eighty years down the line from being inspected. If you'd be so kind as to lend your support on this little matter, we can get them bumped a ways up the schedule. Unless they find something <i>really</i> dangerous in there, I could guarantee you could be digging into them by this time next year.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Even if some Sidereals' intrinsic benefits are relatively cynical like, &quot;It will elevate my standing in the Faction.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T01:14:22-07:00","id":686671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686112#post686112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bronze Vision (at least as presented in the 1st and 2nd edition Sidereal books) showed that the vision requires the Solar Exalted to continually be hunted down and killed or trapped away.<br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> This is part of the reason why the Bronze Vision appears, on its face, to have failed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Vision isn\u2019t the same as how the Bronze Faction decided to act on the vision or what they hoped to accomplish by actualizing it.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals looked into the future and one possibility they saw was of the Solar Exalted being slaughtered by the Terrestrials at the behest of the Sidereals. The Solars would be captured and Creation would diminish under the dragon-blooded rulership.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the vision said \u2018and this will last forever.\u2019<br /> <br /> A vision isn\u2019t a failure or a success; it\u2019s true or false. The Bronze Vision, Darkness Vision, and Gold Vision were all true, only the Bronze and Darkness Visions offered sure outcomes while the Gold Vision had a bunch of unsure ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686386#post686386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This hasn't been true since maybe before the Usurpation, what with all the &quot;getting killed by Lunars&quot; that very frequently goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/oUBRXqY.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 10-03-2015, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T02:24:09-07:00","id":686729,"title":"","content":"[quote=AnubisXy]The Bronze Vision (at least as presented in the 1st] Are you sure about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T03:13:37-07:00","id":686737,"title":"","content":"The idea that the visions stand in perpetuity, valid stretching forever into the future from when they were made, hasn't ever actually been made in the text, I think. People like Chejop keep the faith they made the right choice, but there is no guarantee that choice is valid forever (the Sidereals are not *that* amazing as prophets).<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, this interpretation came from the fan community, as a extra source of legitimacy for the Solars - if the Vision of Bronze is valid forever, then the only hope of a better world lies with the Solars (Visions of the Lunars taking over the world and changing it for the better than under the Dragonblooded etc are ruled out by the Vision of Bronze, etc.)<br /> <br /> And also because fans were interested in this dilemma being present throughout the gameline, not a choice the Sidereals faced at one time in the world history.<br /> <br /> Now, I think this is, while some may find it desirable, it is in a way, actually sort of unnecessary for Solars characters to have legitimacy and tenability.<br /> <br /> Even if empires and the Realm do *not* and have *not* worked at all like many people here have the impression they did, politically and economically, the Realm has done a bad enough job and is oppressive and corrupt enough that there is plenty of material for national liberation struggles and alternative imperial structures under charismatic millennialist cult leaders for Solars to seize on and lead and get caught up within.<br /> <br /> The Solars don't really *need* some &quot;World doesn't improve without us, ever; Vision o' Bronze sez&quot; line for legitimacy when they have the tenuous legitimacy of the Realm, and when they have simple self defense as well, and their own might.<br /> <br /> And I am not sure how keen I am on Exalted of the &quot;No metaplot; but exactly two or three possible broadly defined futures&quot; sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T03:42:09-07:00","id":686741,"title":"","content":"Here's my rough guesses at the Sidereal census...<br /> <br /> Bronze Faction (including both those ideologically in said camp, and those who accept Chejop &amp; allies as the powers that be): 41<br /> Gold Faction (those who actively cast themselves in opposition to the current status-quo in support of some role for returning Solars): 25<br /> Independents (those who actively reject the above duality and attempt to focus solely on their Bureau duties in order to remain apart from it): 25<br /> Ronin (those who don't work for Heaven, includes Rakan Thulio and the Green Lady): 7-9<br /> Silver Faction: if they exist at all, its like one or two guys...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-03-2015, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T05:34:07-07:00","id":686877,"title":"","content":"glamourweaver: &quot;Powers that be.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T06:00:29-07:00","id":686885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686877#post686877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">glamourweaver: &quot;Powers that be.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know it was a grammatical... never mind, joke didn't land...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T09:23:10-07:00","id":687165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686327#post686327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact is, in this game (or in the setting), there should be no such thing as a guaranteed outcome, and there certainly shouldn't be one hundreds to thousands of years in advance just because an Exalt used their magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>We invoked <i>Of Truths Best Unspoken </i> and witnessed that this post might come to pass; we offered sacrifices to Mercury, Venus and Saturn and asked <i>Of Things Desired And Feared</i>. A post is a small price to remind the fandom that Sidereal prophecy has always dealt in certain outcomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T09:29:33-07:00","id":687176,"title":"","content":"I think the Visions could not have been valid in perpetuity, even if they could have predicted all things outside of fate as well. But I think all 99 Sidereals (not counting that one 6-year-old who wasn't in the room) <b><i>assumed</i></b> that all 3 Visions would be valid without alterations for eternity, and therefore none of them would require any replacement, even when random shit from outside of fate drastically changes everything.<br /> <br /> This results in the Sidereals, 1500 years and two horrendous apocalypses later, still arguing over the 2 original Visions and not questioning whether they're still actually relevant or accurate -- as depicted in 2E. Or at least the elders still stuck in that frame of mind, clinging to the certainty that their original choices were self-evidently correct -- creating an institutional inertia (political patronage, organization, received wisdom, etc.) that snares the younger ones even though the young ones are much more able to see the situation with fresh eyes and notice that not everything lines up with what they've been told. Or are possibly more concerned with questions other than &quot;Solars, Yay or Nay?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-03-2015, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T11:47:55-07:00","id":687337,"title":"","content":"Stick with me, cause I have a point at the end about Sidereal prognostication and the visions.<br /> <br /> There's a show called <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/36740473\" target=\"_blank\">Bar Rescue</a>, where the host goes into various bars around the USA that are failing and he tries to fix them. He talks about the science of building a bar and how if you look at the surrounding community and design the floor plan this way and put lights here and make certain kinds of drinks and train your employees in a specific manner and do this and that and a bunch of other things, you can make a successful business.<br /> <br /> I see Heaven's and the Sidereal fate planning whoo whoo as that kind of social science writ large and backed by magic. Collectively, they've had a largely unbroken trail of paperwork with files on everything and everyone that's existed since before the fall of the Primordials through the Great Contagion. The vast vast majority of these files are extremely minimal with most of their information being references to other files, but collectively they were excellent ways to measure trends on extremely long term time scales. When a Heavenly Committee plans the fate of a region of Creation, they decide on what they want to happen, then they look at their files and figure out what the trends exist and they look up how to manipulate those trends to produce the desired end goal. Essence users and things outside of fate mess this up because it's a whole lot harder to get that kind of far reaching trend data on individuals and those who aren't plugged into Heaven's observation matrix (the loom). It gets dressed up with a lot of whoo whoo and pageantry because it's the aesthetic of Heaven and Exalted.<br /> <br /> The Visions were the Sidereals sitting down, taking all their paperwork on the Exalted Host and trying to wring trends out of it, believing that deeper wells of information could replace broader pools, the files on each Exalt are most definitely more detailed, after all. In the end, the Vision of Gold was backed by Sidereals pointing out that broadly, they were all Heroes! Each one made Creation better somehow! They pointed out long and detailed lists of horrible threat that the exalted host had defeated and pulled up charts detailing projected losses that had been averted with Celestial effort. The ones backing the Vision of Bronze pointed out the trends for them all to go bad and how as they age and grow in strength. They provided charts about projected losses and danger to creation - You can look at bright Shattered Ice's past and see how her cold and callousness blossomed from occasional cruelty all the way to building a society where failing to be happy enough is a thought crime punishable by murder. You can look at the Hierarch and see how his overabundance of compassion twists into isolationism so he isn't constantly locked into inaction because someone somewhere is suffering. You can look at a dawn and see how recklessness in youth ends up becoming a trend of getting millions killed in wars of honor and ego as she ages and grows in power.<br /> <br /> The sids don't know about the great curse obviously, but they could see the trends it caused. Someone at Essence 2 who flips out with Red Rage of Compassion has a largely minimal impact on Creation but eventually they'll become older and more powerful, with a great deal more reach and responsibility. I imagine a lot of people, not just Sidereals, had sleepless nights when they thought of someone who has a history of flipping out and causing a lot of damage because cruelty offends them when they ALSO had command of various Areal Battleships or, Sol Forbid, their finger on the button of a Thousand Forged Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T12:56:38-07:00","id":687413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=686671#post686671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bronze Vision isn\u2019t the same as how the Bronze Faction decided to act on the vision or what they hoped to accomplish by actualizing it.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals looked into the future and one possibility they saw was of the Solar Exalted being slaughtered by the Terrestrials at the behest of the Sidereals. The Solars would be captured and Creation would diminish under the dragon-blooded rulership.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the vision said \u2018and this will last forever.\u2019<br /> <br /> A vision isn\u2019t a failure or a success; it\u2019s true or false. The Bronze Vision, Darkness Vision, and Gold Vision were all true, only the Bronze and Darkness Visions offered sure outcomes while the Gold Vision had a bunch of unsure ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>And so far the Bronze Faction's overwhelming response to the Bronze Vision no longer being &quot;true&quot; (or valid or functional or however you want to describe it) is to stubbornly bury their heads in the sand and go, &quot;Nuh uh! It's totally still valid!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it would be nice if the Bronze Faction Sidereal Exalted were presented as a little more proactive and coming up with solutions or new ways to save Creation from the threat of the Solars, rather than present the readers with the idea that their only plan is to keep doing the same things they've always done, even though that course is clearly no longer feasible. Even just a few pie-in-sky ideas that aren't possible might show them as adaptable and present them in a slightly more positive light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T03:11:30-07:00","id":689528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions?p=687413#post687413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And so far the Bronze Faction's overwhelming response to the Bronze Vision no longer being &quot;true&quot; (or valid or functional or however you want to describe it) is to stubbornly bury their heads in the sand and go, &quot;Nuh uh! It's totally still valid!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it would be nice if the Bronze Faction Sidereal Exalted were presented as a little more proactive and coming up with solutions or new ways to save Creation from the threat of the Solars, rather than present the readers with the idea that their only plan is to keep doing the same things they've always done, even though that course is clearly no longer feasible. Even just a few pie-in-sky ideas that aren't possible might show them as adaptable and present them in a slightly more positive light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe it's their turn to fall?<br /> <br /> Exalted runs on this premise that whomever holds power will eventually succumb to complacency and hubris. First the Primordials, then the Solars. At this point, the Bronze Faction is, in effect, the next ones in line. They spend 1500 or so years running with the &quot;kill the other Celestials&quot; plan. They kept to that plan even after the Contagion, even after the Crusade. They have accepted all the &quot;prices&quot; demanded of the vision of Bronze.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly in setting, and perfectly in tune with the Bronze Faction's make-up, to flail around a little bit. Chejop is certainly flailing around, He put all his chips on Big Red, and she's gone. The Bronzies don't get a pass on the shit end of their Great Curse. I think the intent is that if the Bronze Faction will survive, it will require PC intervention. It's an organization that is ripe for a new direction, and new leadership.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say the Bronze Faction will all be slaughtered, censored, or anything like that. Many of the younger and &quot;middle-aged&quot; ones will simply view it as a failed plan, and migrate either to the Gold Faction or the Indies. Or they will defect to a PC-founded organization. It's mostly the Elders who are truly invested in the idea,. as they remember the First Age and fear it, or they remember the High Shogunate, and miss it. The much diminished Bronze Faction goes out with a whimper, rather than a bang. Chejop has that heart attack. Anys Syn dies fighting a Circle of Solars alongside her best Terrestrial students. And that's it.<br /> <br /> It could go any number of ways, but I think it's important for the default setting to allow the path of least resistance to be that it's time for Chejop and his cohorts to pay the piper, one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T06:59:52-07:00","id":689653,"title":"","content":"Even if a Solar (there is no <i>the</i> Solars the way there is the Sidereals, the Lunars or the Dragon Blooded) was to bring down the Realm and rearrange the power of the Sidereals over affairs in Creation, it may still be that Creation is too far gone to fall under their power again.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty huge &quot;if&quot; though; the Realm is strong.<br /> <br /> I also see the degree to which people ascribe a cyclical monomyth to Creation to be about as weird as them doing it to real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:16:58-07:00","id":689744,"title":"","content":"I don't think a cyclical monomyth is necessarily baked into Creation -- it doesn't seem to have applied to anything before the Primordial War. But if the Exalted keep using the same &quot;Overthrow, No Mercy, No Compromise, No Reconciliation&quot; methods, I think they'll keep getting the same results: war, degeneration, the cosmos getting more and more broken. Eventually that probably destroys the world or reduces it to an uninhabitable cinder.<br /> <br /> Now maybe that's part of the Great Curse and breaking that would change the course of the &quot;Overthrow and Murder Everyone&quot; approach, but judging by how well violent revolutions and genocide usually turn out in real life, I doubt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}